{"level":30,"time":1778519955627,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_014qAwae9mNMsA9E6qZKV1u5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I have the grouping file. Now I need to understand this grouping:\n\n**Grouping 2: Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines**\n\nThis grouping covers tree placement requirements near overhead electric distribution and transmission lines. The key things I need to understand:\n\n1. **Voltage Classification**: \n   - Distribution: < 60kV (typical 12.47kV, 34.5kV)\n   - Transmission: ≥ 60kV (69kV, 138kV, 345kV)\n\n2. **Key Thresholds**:\n   - Utility-compatible trees (UC designation in ECM Appendix F): \n     - Within < 15 ft of distribution: only utility-compatible trees\n     - Within 15-25 ft of distribution: utility-compatible OR trees with mature height < 40 ft\n     - Within > 25 ft of distribution: all trees permitted\n     - Within < 50 ft of transmission: only utility-compatible trees\n   - Large trees (≥ 40 ft mature height):\n     - Within < 25 ft of distribution: prohibited\n     - Within < 50 ft of transmission: prohibited\n   - Additional prohibitions (all tree types):\n     - Within transmission easement boundaries\n     - Within 10 ft of any electric utility pole\n     - Within 10 ft of pad-mounted equipment\n     - Within 5 ft of underground electric equipment\n   - Root barriers required for trees within 20 ft of underground equipment\n\n3. **Measurement**: All clearances measured as lateral (horizontal) distance from tree trunk center to outside conductor (not pole centerline or structure).\n\n4. **Checklist Items**: 15 items (EL-2.1 through EL-2.15)\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Check applicability (does this project have overhead electric facilities?)\n2. Research the site plan to find:\n   - Overhead electric distribution and transmission line locations\n   - Tree locations and species\n   - Plant schedule/legend\n   - Any transmission easements\n   - Any pad-mounted or underground electric equipment\n3. Evaluate each checklist item\n\nLet me start by reading the README to understand the project and then check facts.md for applicability.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3753,"cache_read_input_tokens":24713,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3753},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dedcba6e-469f-4ff1-8623-d3aaae962125","uuid":"6414c33e-63c5-49a4-aa6a-54b621f19f45"}
