rizontally along the entire bottom boundary of the site plan drawing.\n\n**Are there any trees or plantings shown near them?**\nYes. While the left and middle portions of the \"-OHE-\" line appear relatively clear of plantings, the right portion of the line has several trees shown near or directly intersecting it. Specifically:\n*   Towards the bottom right side of the plan, the \"-OHE-\" line passes directly through a large tree canopy symbol.\n*   Just to the left of this large intersecting canopy, there is a smaller tree symbol containing the letter **\"M\"**. According to the notes below the KEY NOTES section, \"M\" stands for **\"M - MITIGATION TREE\"**. This proposed mitigation tree is located immediately adjacent to the overhead electric line.\n*   Further to the right, near the bottom right corner where the \"-OHE-\" line ends or exits the view, there are additional tree symbols, including one with a callout labeled **\"H8\"**."}]}
