{"level":30,"time":1778520458567,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01NQoN9CMzAhxtMwpmG6C5HF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! Now I have confirmed that there ARE existing overhead electric lines on the site along the western boundary adjacent to Valley View Road. These are the existing facilities that the proposed development must maintain clearances from. Now I need to:\n\n1. Check all the proposed site features to see if they maintain required clearances\n2. Examine all relevant sheets where these clearances should be documented\n3. Evaluate all 47 checklist items\n\nThe key findings so far:\n- Existing overhead electric lines (O.H.E.) run north-south along the western boundary\n- Multiple utility poles exist along this boundary\n- Guy wires are attached to the poles\n- Lines branch across Valley View Road\n\nNow I need to check:\n1. Whether the proposed buildings maintain required clearances from these lines\n2. Whether the proposed driveways/parking maintain required vertical clearances\n3. Whether the proposed landscaping maintains required tree clearances\n4. Whether profile/elevation sheets show the required clearance documentation\n5. Whether the plans include proper notation about the 48-hour notification requirement\n6. Whether there's a transmission easement on the site (based on the transmission notes in Sheet 3)\n\nLet me check the site plan (Sheet 9) to see the relationship between the proposed buildings and the overhead electric lines.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":574,"cache_read_input_tokens":57222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":574},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":