{"level":30,"time":1778521249694,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011hYtAZrMeJg9HvdSjwf817","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"It looks like the blocks.md file I have is incomplete. The guide.md mentioned Blocks 13, 14, 16, 17, 19 that should contain various notes and approvals, but they don't appear in the blocks.md file I read. This might be a limitation of the blocks.md extraction.\n\nLet me proceed with what I have and focus on the key findings so far:\n\nFrom my research, I have found:\n1. Transformer pads ARE shown on Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan)\n2. Transformer pads ARE shown with clearances to buildings adequate for the 5-foot minimum (EL-13.1 PASSES)\n3. Access door orientations are NOT marked on the plans (per vision tool findings)\n4. Transformer pad dimensions do NOT appear to be specified on the plans (no callouts visible)\n5. Bollards are NOT shown on the plans (but may not be required if pads are > 4 feet from parking/traffic)\n6. Transformer easements are NOT specifically shown as a separate easement exhibit\n7. General note says \"Additional electric easements may be required at a later date\" (suggesting they haven't been fully coordinated)\n\nThe question is: what level of detail is required for a \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\"? The sheet is labeled \"Preliminary,\" suggesting it's not final design. This might affect whether certain detailed requirements (like AE Design-approved pad dimensions, access door markings, bollards, etc.) are expected to be shown at this stage.\n\nHowever, the checklist items don't distinguish between preliminary and final design - they require certain elements to be shown. So I need to evaluate them based on what's expected in a submittable site plan.\n\nKey issues I can identify:\n1. EL-13.10 and EL-13.11: Hot-stick clearances are not verifiable without access door orientation marked\n2. EL-13.4: Reduced clearances not documented with AE Design approval\n\n\n3. Several items lack supporting documentation: niche configurations aren't noted, cross-sections showing vertical clearances are missing, transformer easements aren't delineated, and pad dimensions don't align with AE Design details. I should also verify the grading plan to confirm whether oil-filled transformers are specified and if drainage slopes direct water away from buildings as required.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":269,"cache_read_input_tokens":59710,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":269},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64cdee63-31dd-4baa-841a-32fa24fe3ff6","uuid":"2c0d47d2-0631-4a17-9f32-1233a5087e94"}
