{"level":30,"time":1778522596136,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L8Nrgyvp4UK1vrGDjftdCn","type":"tool_result","content":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a meeting.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (ph 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be laydown curbing.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:  · any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:## text_block: Additional notes outlining requirements from Austin Energy regarding easements, tree work, erosion control, and safety clearances. Contains information regarding the developer's responsibility for tree pruning, erosion control, and maintaining clearances according to safety codes.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electrical facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:## text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements for tree pruning, easements, clearances, and relocation costs.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless require clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:*   **Block 16:** Electric Transmission Notes. READ for critical safety clearances, structural load requirements for roads in easements, and barricade rules required by Austin Energy.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:*   **Blocks 14 & 18:** Electric Notes and Austin Energy standard requirements. READ for tree pruning, easement access, and code compliance constraints.\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:- `block-17.md` — text_block: Additional notes outlining requirements from Austin Energy regarding easements, tree work, erosion c\n/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:- `block-19.md` — text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9d22de9-3775-4de4-8f1c-3803e38c8ea2","uuid":"3c0dd9ac-f993-4560-a8e6-88489ea10773","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Au