{"level":30,"time":1778523366786,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rvq2U8X9fTy8oHCUvhGUfD","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 11 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — A graphic scale bar indicating that 1 inch equals 20 feet.\n     4→\n     5→[graphic scale bar with increments 0, 20, 40]\n     6→Scale 1\" = 20'\n     7→\n     8→## Block 2: drawing — This is a detailed grading plan for a multi-family development. It shows existing and proposed contours, building footprints, retaining walls, storm drainage infrastructure, and various utility easements. Key features include multiple buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, each with finished floor elevations (FFE). The plan also indicates existing structures, vegetation, and adjacent property information.\n     9→\n    10→The plan displays a comprehensive layout for a multi-family development. It includes:\n    11→\n    12→*   **Building Footprints:** Eight buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, with their respective square footages and finished floor elevations (FFE). For example, Bldg. 1 is 3,290 sf with an FFE of 687.50, and Bldg. 8 is 4,997 sf with an FFE of 685.50.\n    13→*   **Topography:** Existing and proposed contour lines indicating the site's elevation changes.\n    14→*   **Infrastructure:** Proposed storm drain lines, area inlets, and concrete retaining walls.\n    15→*   **Easements:** Various easements are depicted, including drainage easements, wastewater easements, electric and telephone easements, and a greenbelt access and use easement.\n    16→*   **Adjacent Properties:** Information on adjacent properties, such as \"Lot A Cortex Heights Zoning: MF 3-CO Use: Multi-Family\" and \"William Lance Corsbie, Jr. 1.967 Acres Zoning: SF-3 Use: Single Family\".\n    17→*   **Existing Features:** Existing trees, rock rubble, and stone retaining walls.\n    18→*   **Utilities:** Locations of existing water manholes, gas meters, wastewater manholes, and AT&T vaults.\n    19→*   **Specific Details:** The plan includes specific details like a sediment basin, an existing retaining wall to be replaced, and a sidewalk easement.\n    20→\n    21→## Block 3: notes — Provides the legal description of the property being developed.\n    22→\n    23→Legal Description\n    24→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    25→\n    26→## Block 4: notes — A brief note directing the reader to another sheet for a list of trees.\n    27→\n    28→Tree List\n    29→Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n    30→\n    31→## Block 5: notes — This is the legend for the grading plan, explaining the symbols and line types used to represent various features on the drawing, such as contours, spot elevations, curbs, limits of construction, storm drains, level landings, and ADA ramps.\n    32→\n    33→Legend\n    34→[dashed line] --700-- Existing Contour\n    35→[solid line] --700-- Proposed Contour\n    36→[plus sign] 698.25 Proposed Spot Elevation\n    37→700.00\n    38→699.50 Top of Curb\n    39→Bottom of Curb\n    40→[solid line with LOC] Proposed Limits of Construction\n    41→[dashed line with SD] Proposed Storm Drain Line\n    42→L= Level Landing\n    43→(Not to exceed 2% in any Direction)\n    44→Down [arrow] ADA Ramp\n    45→(Not to exceed 8.33%)\n    46→\n    47→## Block 6: notes — A note providing specific instructions regarding the construction of grading lines related to curbs.\n    48→\n    49→Curb Note:\n    50→Grading lines that indicate flows toward the curb shall be constructed as a catch curb. Grade lines that indicate flows\n    51→away from curb shall be constructed as a spill curb.\n    52→\n    53→## Block 7: notes — Details two benchmark points used for elevation reference on the site plan.\n    54→\n    55→Benchmarks\n    56→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    57→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    58→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    59→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    60→\n    61→## Block 11: text_block — A general disclaimer stating that the application does not constitute verification of all data, and the engineer of record is responsible for its completeness and accuracy.\n    62→\n    63→Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the\n    64→applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her\n    65→submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n    66→\n    67→## Block 13: text_block — A note advising that existing utility locations are based on record information and must be field-verified by the contractor prior to construction.\n    68→\n    69→The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not\n    70→match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility\n    71→locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning\n    72→construction.\n    73→\n    74→## Block 14: text_block — A clear instruction to call before starting any excavation work.\n    75→\n    76→Call Before You Dig!!\n    77→\n    78→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dedcba6e-469f-4ff1-8623-d3aaae962125","uuid":"3053fb32-42d2-4c73-9550-c74a4f306867","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 11 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — A graphic scale bar indicating that 1 inch equals 20 feet.\n\n[graphic scale bar with increments 0, 20, 40]\nScale 1\" = 20'\n\n## Block 2: drawing — This is a detailed grading plan for a multi-family development. It shows existing and proposed contours, building footprints, retaining walls, storm drainage infrastructure, and various utility easements. Key features include multiple buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, each with finished floor elevations (FFE). The plan also indicates existing structures, vegetation, and adjacent property information.\n\nThe plan displays a comprehensive layout for a multi-family development. It includes:\n\n*   **Building Footprints:** Eight buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, with their respective square footages and finished floor elevations (FFE). For example, Bldg. 1 is 3,290 sf with an FFE of 687.50, and Bldg. 8 is 4,997 sf with an FFE of 685.50.\n*   **Topography:** Existing and proposed contour lines indicating the site's elevation changes.\n*   **Infrastructure:** Proposed storm drain lines, area inlets, and concrete retaining walls.\n*   **Easements:** Various easements are depicted, including drainage easements, wastewater easements, electric and telephone easements, and a greenbelt access and use easement.\n*   **Adjacent Properties:** Information on adjacent properties, such as \"Lot A Cortex Heights Zoning: MF 3-CO Use: Multi-Family\" and \"William Lance Corsbie, Jr. 1.967 Acres Zoning: SF-3 Use: Single Family\".\n*   **Existing Features:** Existing trees, rock rubble, and stone retaining walls.\n*   **Utilities:** Locations of existing water manholes, gas meters, wastewater manholes, and AT&T vaults.\n*   **Specific Details:** The plan includes specific details like a sediment basin, an existing retaining wall to be replaced, and a sidewalk easement.\n\n## Block 3: notes — Provides the legal description of the property being developed.\n\nLegal Description\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n## Block 4: notes — A brief note directing the reader to another sheet for a list of trees.\n\nTree List\nRefer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n\n## Block 5: notes — This is the legend for the grading plan, explaining the symbols and line types used to represent various features on the drawing, such as contours, spot elevations, curbs, limits of construction, storm drains, level landings, and ADA ramps.\n\nLegend\n[dashed line] --700-- Existing Contour\n[solid line] --700-- Proposed Contour\n[plus sign] 698.25 Proposed Spot Elevation\n700.00\n699.50 Top of Curb\nBottom of Curb\n[solid line with LOC] Proposed Limits of Construction\n[dashed line with SD] Proposed Storm Drain Line\nL= Level Landing\n(Not to exceed 2% in any Direction)\nDown [arrow] ADA Ramp\n(Not to exceed 8.33%)\n\n## Block 6: notes — A note providing specific instructions regarding the construction of grading lines related to curbs.\n\nCurb Note:\nGrading lines that indicate flows toward the curb shall be constructed as a catch curb. Grade lines that indicate flows\naway from curb shall be constructed as a spill curb.\n\n## Block 7: notes — Details two benchmark points used for elevation reference on the site plan.\n\nBenchmarks\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n## Block 11: text_block — A general disclaimer stating that the application does not constitute verification of all data, and the engineer of record is responsible for its completeness and accuracy.\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the\napplicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her\nsubmittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\n## Block 13: text_block — A note advising that existing utility locations are based on record information and must be field-verified by the contractor prior to construction.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not\nmatch locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility\nlocations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning\nconstruction.\n\n## Block 14: text_block — A clear instruction to call before starting any excavation work.\n\nCall Before You Dig!!\n\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778523366786,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_017YRPVfdhVKZtYPQTW6VbCK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the grading plan mentions \"electric and telephone easements\" but no mention of transmission easements. The electric easements are likely the 5-foot electric easements mentioned in facts.md, which are typically underground distribution easements, not transmission.\n\nNow let me summarize what I've found about the OHE (Overhead Electric) line:\n\n**Facts about Overhead Electric Facilities:**\n1. OHE line runs along the southern (bottom) boundary of the site (Valley View Road side)\n2. OHE line is labeled as \"- OHE -\" on the landscape plan\n3. Multiple trees are positioned within 15 feet of this OHE line:\n   - 0.7 feet away (scalloped symbol with M and dot)\n   - 1 foot away (symbol with + and M)\n   - 1.5 feet away (grey shaded canopy)\n   - 6 feet away (scalloped symbol with M)\n   - 11 feet away (symbol with + and E)\n\n**Tree Species Information from Plant Schedule (Sheet 35):**\n- Shade Trees: Live Oak (circle with +), Cedar Elm (circle with dot)\n- Ornamental Trees: Texas Mountain Laurel (scalloped circle with dot), Mexican Redbud (circle with scalloped shape and branch line)\n- Shrubs: Dwarf Palmetto, Big Muhly, Gulf Muhly, Texas Sage, Dwarf Wax Myrtle\n- Mitigation Trees: Species NOT identified in plant schedule (marked only with 'M')\n\n**Issues Identified:**\n\n1. **EL-2.10 - FAIL**: Plant legend or plant schedule does not identify species of trees proposed near electric facilities\n   - The mitigation trees ('M' symbols) near the OHE line are NOT identified by species in the plant schedule\n   - Without species identification, cannot verify utility compatibility (ECM Appendix F)\n   \n2. **EL-2.11 - FAIL**: The plant schedule only provides minimum installation heights (16', 8', 10'), not mature heights, so I cannot determine which trees qualify as large trees (40+ feet at maturity per ECM Appendix F). Cedar Elm and Live Oak likely reach 40+ feet but this isn't specified on the plans.\n\n3. **EL-2.1 - NOT-VERIFIABLE**: Since multiple trees are planted within 15 feet of the OHE line and I cannot verify their species or mature heights, I cannot confirm they're compatible with utility requirements.\n\n4. **EL-2.3 - NOT-VERIFIABLE**: Trees within 25 feet of the OHE line cannot be verified without mature height data, which is missing from the documentation.\n\n5. **EL-2.14 - PASS**: The OHE line and trees are both shown on the landscape plan in relation to each other, though the clarity for verification is limited.\n\n6. **EL-2.12, EL-2.13 - Not applicable**: These standards apply only when clearance dimensions are provided, which they are not here.\n\nNow I need to evaluate the remaining standards (EL-2.2, EL-2.4, EL-2.5, EL-2.6, EL-2.7, EL-2.8, EL-2.9, EL-2.15) by checking whether transmission facilities, utility poles, pad-mounted equipment, or underground equipment are shown or proposed on the plan.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1719,"cache_read_input_tokens":62824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1719},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dedcba6e-469f-4ff1-8623-d3aaae962125","uuid":"2bd29a5c-7055-434d-a407-8c0bcb5b6dc5"}
