13.24-25: Gas and other utility line separations need checking\n- EL-13.26: Utilities crossing above or below transformer locations\n- EL-13.27-28: Overhead line clearances still require assessment\n- EL-13.29-31: Niche configurations and cross-sections appear not applicable\n\nGrading and drainage provisions for oil-filled equipment need verification. Property boundaries and easement locations should be confirmed against the design. Transformer pad dimensions must align with architectural specifications. Bollard protection isn't needed since pads maintain adequate distance from parking areas. I should verify whether any structures span above or below the overhead distribution lines. Gas service availability to the site is a key factor to determine next.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1685,"cache_read_input_tokens":67600,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1685},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64cdee63-31dd-4baa-841a-32fa24fe3ff6","uuid":"b7f6ca15-d61d-439f-9242-a75118748c26"}
