ly. The requirement to measure from tree trunk is not addressed on the plans at all. No evidence of measurement methodology is present.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric line along southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees and OHE line on same drawing, allowing basic spatial relationship verification. However, the relationship cannot be adequately verified because: (1) no clearance dimensions provided; (2) utility pole locations not clearly marked; (3) conductor positions (outside edge of conductors) not shown; (4) no cross-reference to electrical utility plan showing existing vs. proposed utilities. Clarity of utility infrastructure on landscape plan is insufficient for independent clearance verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows both OHE line and tree symbols but lacks dimensional callouts, pole markers, conductor edge locations, and cross-references to utility plans. Vision check confirmed trees are shown adjacent to OHE but without documentation of clearance.","reasoning":"While trees and utilities appear on the same drawing, the documentation is incomplete. Utilities must be shown with sufficient detail (pole locations, conductor positions, dimensional clearances) to verify compliance. Bare line representation without dimensional or structural detail is insufficient for verification.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees shown adjacent to OHE line on landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-