{"level":30,"time":1778523688503,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":3713797,"duration_api_ms":154861,"num_turns":31,"result":"I've completed the comprehensive site plan review for Grouping 2: **Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines**.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n**Key Applicability Determinations:**\n- **Overhead electric distribution lines:** Present (existing \"OHE\" line shown on Landscape Plan, Sheet 31)\n- **Transmission facilities:** Not found on site documentation\n- **Trees near utilities:** Yes - multiple trees proposed adjacent to overhead electric line\n\n**Critical Deficiencies Identified:**\n\n| Deficiency | Status | Key Issue |\n|-----------|--------|-----------|\n| EL-2.3 | **FAIL** | Large trees (Cedar Elm 40-50 ft, Live Oak 40-80 ft) shown directly adjacent to OHE distribution line without clearance dimensions |\n| EL-2.10 | **FAIL** | Tree species not labeled directly on landscape plan drawing; species only in separate plant schedule |\n| EL-2.11 | **FAIL** | Large trees not differentiated on landscape plan to distinguish them from smaller trees |\n| EL-2.14 | **FAIL** | Landscape plan shows trees and OHE together but lacks dimensional callouts, pole locations, and conductor edge positions needed for verification |\n| EL-2.1 | **NOT-VERIFIABLE** | Plant schedule lists species but does not verify utility-compatible status against ECM Appendix F |\n| EL-2.6 | **NOT-VERIFIABLE** | Utility pole locations not clearly marked on landscape plan with dimensions to proposed trees |\n| EL-2.8, EL-2.9 | **NOT-VERIFIABLE** | Underground utilities and root barrier details not cross-referenced on landscape plan |\n| EL-2.12, EL-2.13 | **NOT-VERIFIABLE** | No clearance dimensions shown; measurement methodology cannot be verified |\n| EL-2.15 | **NOT-VERIFIABLE** | No Austin Energy written approval documented for trees potentially in restricted zones |\n\n**Items marked N/A:**\n- EL-2.2, EL-2.4, EL-2.5: No transmission facilities present on site\n- EL-2.7: Cannot confirm pad-mounted equipment presence\n\nThe primary concern is that the landscape plan shows large trees positioned directly along the existing overhead electric distribution line without any documentation of clearances, species utility-compatibility, or Austin Energy approval.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5a0afb9f-ba74-482f-b16b-de22c2cb4f07","total_cost_usd":0.26459225,"usage":{"input_tokens":157,"cache_creation_input_tokens":54365,"cache_read_input_tokens":1191840,"output_tokens":15459,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":54365,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":157,"outputTokens":15459,"cacheReadInputTokens":1191840,"cacheCreationInputTokens":54365,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.26459225,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric distribution line, southern property boundary near proposed mitigation trees"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plant schedule (Sheet 35) identifies species proposed near OHE line but does not verify utility-compatible status against ECM Appendix F UC column. Landscape plan shows trees adjacent to OHE but provides no clearance dimensions or documentation confirming compliance with 15-foot distribution clearance requirement. Cannot verify whether trees meet utility-compatibility criteria without ECM Appendix F reference.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) depicts OHE line with adjacent tree symbols; plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists 20 proposed trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) but does not cite ECM Appendix F or mark any as utility-compatible. No clearance dimensions or measurements are provided on landscape plan.","reasoning":"The deficiency cannot be confirmed as pass because no explicit verification of utility-compatible status appears on plans or in plant schedule. The deficiency cannot be confirmed as fail because the tree species are shown but their compliance category is not documented. This is a documentation gap rather than confirmable non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead transmission lines (≥60kV) are shown or documented on site plan or grading plan. Narrow electric easements shown (5-foot) indicate distribution infrastructure. While General Notes (Sheet 3) contain transmission-related requirements, no transmission facilities are depicted on submitted plans, and facts.md contains no record of transmission easement. Transmission tree clearance requirements do not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows only 5-foot electric easements; facts.md lists no transmission easement; vision check of Sheet 11 found no transmission lines or structures labeled. General Notes contain transmission requirements but as apparent boilerplate.","reasoning":"For EL-2.2 to be applicable, transmission facilities must be present or proposed. The evidence indicates distribution-only infrastructure (narrow easements, no transmission structures shown). Therefore, this item is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along existing overhead electric distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plant schedule proposes 10 Cedar Elm (typical mature height 40-50 ft) and 2 Live Oak (typical mature height 40-80 ft) trees. These exceed the 40-foot mature height threshold for large trees per ECM Appendix F. Landscape plan shows trees adjacent to OHE line but does not provide clearance dimensions demonstrating compliance with 25-foot large tree clearance requirement. Large trees are not differentiated on plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists Cedar Elm at 100-gallon size (mature height ~40-50 ft) and Live Oak at 100-gallon size (mature height ~40-80 ft) positioned near OHE line. Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows these trees (marked M for mitigation) directly along OHE line. No clearance dimensions provided.","reasoning":"Cedar Elm and Live Oak are species with documented mature heights ≥40 feet, meeting the ECM large tree definition. The landscape plan shows them positioned on or immediately adjacent to the OHE line without distance callouts. At 0-5 feet from the distribution line, they violate the 25-foot minimum clearance for large trees. Large trees should be differentiated on plans per EL-2.11; their absence from the plan violates both requirements.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission facilities are present on site; applicability condition not met. See EL-2.2 determination.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading plan and site documentation show distribution easements only; no transmission structures, lines, or easements depicted.","reasoning":"This item applies only when transmission facilities are present. No transmission infrastructure is shown on plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement is shown or identified on grading plan, plat, or utility documentation. Applicability condition not met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading plan shows 5-foot electric easements only; facts.md lists no transmission easement in property records; vision check found no transmission easement labeled.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when a transmission easement exists. No transmission easement is documented as present on this site.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Locations of existing overhead electric utility poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles marked in legend. Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows overhead electric line but does not explicitly locate or dimension utility poles relative to proposed trees. Cannot verify 10-foot clearance from utility pole centerlines without pole locations clearly marked on landscape plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows utility pole symbols in legend; landscape plan (Sheet 31) depicts OHE line but does not show pole locations or dimensions from poles to trees. Proposed trees shown near utility line but pole positions not clearly marked relative to tree symbols.","reasoning":"To verify EL-2.6, utility pole locations must be clearly identified on the landscape plan with dimensions to proposed trees. While poles exist (shown in survey legend), their exact positions and distances from proposed trees are not documented on the landscape plan.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Pad-mounted transformer locations (if present)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electrical infrastructure with transformers and pull boxes, but not pad-mounted above-ground equipment. Landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not reference pad-mount equipment locations. Cannot confirm whether pad-mounted equipment exists on site; applicability cannot be determined.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) describes underground transformers and pull boxes; landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not show pad-mounted transformer symbols or locations. Utility plan references show underground infrastructure.","reasoning":"EL-2.7 applies only if pad-mounted equipment is present. The electrical infrastructure shown is underground, suggesting no above-ground pad-mounts. However, the site might have existing pad-mounts not addressed in the new electrical design. This cannot be definitively determined from the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Underground electric utility locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) indicates underground electric lines and pull boxes but does not show underground equipment locations in relation to landscape plan. Landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not cross-reference underground utility locations. Cannot verify 5-foot clearance from underground equipment without documented equipment locations on landscape plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electric lines and pull boxes; landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not show underground utility locations or dimensions to proposed trees. Plans not cross-referenced.","reasoning":"To verify EL-2.8, underground equipment locations must be shown on the landscape plan with clearance dimensions to nearby trees. The electrical plan shows infrastructure but not its spatial relationship to landscaping on the landscape plan itself.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Underground electric equipment (if present near proposed trees)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No documentation of underground equipment within 20-foot proximity of proposed trees on landscape plan. No root barrier details or specifications shown on landscape plan or detail sheets. Cannot verify compliance without underground utility locations documented on landscape plan and corresponding root barrier details shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not overlay underground utility locations; no root barrier details visible on landscape plan or referenced detail sheets for trees near underground utilities. Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows underground systems but not in relation to proposed plantings.","reasoning":"EL-2.9 requires identification of trees within 20 feet of underground equipment AND verification of 4-foot-deep root barriers positioned 5 feet from equipment. Neither the proximity identification nor the barrier specifications are documented on the landscape plan.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed tree locations near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees near OHE line with symbols (M, SY, PL) but does not directly label species on the drawing. Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists species but is a separate document. The landscape plan itself lacks direct species identification at tree locations, making it difficult to cross-reference species to utility compatibility without consulting separate schedule. Direct species labeling on landscape plan is required for verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols (M, SY, PL, P) but not species names at those locations. Plant schedule on separate sheet (35) lists species in tabular form. Near the OHE line, trees are shown but not labeled by species on the landscape drawing itself.","reasoning":"While species are documented in the plant schedule, they are not identified directly on the landscape plan at the tree locations. Reviewer Convention requires species identification at tree locations, not solely in a separate table. Cross-referencing symbols to a separate schedule adds verification difficulty and increases risk of error.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed trees near overhead electric distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees (Cedar Elm and Live Oak, both 40+ foot mature height) proposed near OHE line are not differentiated on landscape plan. Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists mature heights in tabular form but this information is not reflected on the landscape plan drawing itself. Large trees must be visually distinguishable on the landscape plan to allow rapid verification of clearance requirements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols (M, SY, etc.) uniformly without size differentiation. Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists mature heights (Cedar Elm ~40-50 ft, Live Oak ~40-80 ft) but this information is not indicated on the landscape plan drawing. Large tree designation should be visible on the plan itself.","reasoning":"ECM and clearance requirements distinguish large trees (40+ ft) from smaller trees, requiring different clearance distances. Landscape plans must visually differentiate large trees to enable field verification and compliance checking. Referencing separate sheets defeats this purpose.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees shown on landscape plan near OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on landscape plan between trees and OHE line. Therefore, the measurement reference point (conductor vs. pole) cannot be verified. Vision analysis confirmed trees adjacent to OHE but no dimensional callouts present. If clearances were dimensioned, measurement origin (conductor vs. pole) could not be verified from current plan documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows OHE line with adjacent tree symbols but contains no dimension callouts, arrows, or measurements between trees and the utility line. Without dimensions, the measurement methodology cannot be assessed.","reasoning":"While this deficiency addresses measurement methodology IF dimensions are shown, the absence of any clearance dimensions prevents verification that the methodology is correct. The requirement remains applicable (trees ARE near utilities) but measurement reference cannot be evaluated without dimensional callouts on the plan.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees shown on landscape plan near OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on landscape plan. Similar to EL-2.12, the absence of dimensional callouts means the measurement reference point (trunk vs. canopy) cannot be verified. If dimensions were provided, the origin point (tree trunk center vs. canopy edge) could be assessed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows tree symbols near OHE line but no dimension callouts or measurement references. Without dimensional annotations, measurement methodology and reference points cannot be verified.","reasoning":"This deficiency is not-verifiable rather than pass because measurements are missing entirely. The requirement to measure from tree trunk is not addressed on the plans at all. No evidence of measurement methodology is present.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric line along southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees and OHE line on same drawing, allowing basic spatial relationship verification. However, the relationship cannot be adequately verified because: (1) no clearance dimensions provided; (2) utility pole locations not clearly marked; (3) conductor positions (outside edge of conductors) not shown; (4) no cross-reference to electrical utility plan showing existing vs. proposed utilities. Clarity of utility infrastructure on landscape plan is insufficient for independent clearance verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows both OHE line and tree symbols but lacks dimensional callouts, pole markers, conductor edge locations, and cross-references to utility plans. Vision check confirmed trees are shown adjacent to OHE but without documentation of clearance.","reasoning":"While trees and utilities appear on the same drawing, the documentation is incomplete. Utilities must be shown with sufficient detail (pole locations, conductor positions, dimensional clearances) to verify compliance. Bare line representation without dimensional or structural detail is insufficient for verification.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees shown adjacent to OHE line on landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows trees (especially mitigation trees marked M) directly along OHE line, likely within prohibited clearance zones for large trees. No documentation of Austin Energy written approval is visible on landscape plan, in site plan notes, or in general notes addressing these specific tree locations. Cannot confirm whether approval was obtained or whether planting plan complies without such documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees on/adjacent to OHE line. Reviewed general notes (Sheet 3), site plan (Sheet 9), and all available documentation. No reference to Austin Energy approval letter or correspondence authorizing specific tree plantings within clearance zones is found on any submitted sheet.","reasoning":"If trees are within prohibited zones (as visual evidence suggests for the mitigation trees on OHE line), Austin Energy written approval is required. Such approval should be documented on the plans or attached as correspondence. The complete absence of approval documentation means either: (1) trees are compliant without needing approval, or (2) approval is missing. Without clearance dimensions to determine actual distances, we cannot determine which is true.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a0493e56-1349-4397-bd03-d37bb4a8a39e"}
{"level":30,"time":1778523688503,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01NHbZHNfwJGmBZSRADjTwz8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting - the vision tool says this is Sheet 28, not Sheet 31. But it also confirms that transformer pad locations are NOT labeled on the landscape plan, so I can't determine tree proximities from this sheet. The tree species information would be on a different sheet (likely the Tree List sheet or similar).\n\nLet me now think about my overall findings and compile them into my final output. Let me review what I need to document:\n\nFAILS/NOT-VERIFIABLE ITEMS:\n\n1. **EL-13.21** - FAIL: Transformer pads west of Building 2 (1.4 ft), west of Building 8 (3.7 ft), and east of Building 6 (3.5 ft) lack minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from water lines\n   - Code Citation: UCM § 2.9.1.B.2\n   - Applicable Areas: Site plan near Buildings 2, 8, and 6\n   - Sheet References: Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan)\n\n2. **EL-13.22** - FAIL: Transformer pad west of Building 1 has 4.9 feet clearance from wastewater line, which is less than the 5-foot minimum\n   - Code Citation: UCM § 2.9.1.B.2\n   - Applicable Areas: Site plan near Building 1\n   - Sheet References: Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan)\n\n3. **EL-13.10** - NOT-VERIFIABLE: Hot-stick use area (access door side) clearances cannot be verified because transformer pad access door orientations are not marked or labeled on the electrical plan\n   - Code Citation: UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4\n   - Applicable Areas: All transformer pad locations on Sheet 21\n   - Sheet References: Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan)\n\n4. **EL-13.35** - NOT-VERIFIABLE: Transformer easements aren't depicted on the site plan; general notes reference potential future electric easements. Code Citation: UCM § 1.10.3. Applicable Areas: All transformer pad locations. Sheet References: Sheet 3 (General Notes)\n\n5. **EL-13.37** - NOT-VERIFIABLE: Transformer pad dimensions are not shown on the plans and do not match Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets for the specified transformer type. Code Citation: UCM § 1.10.2. Applicable Areas: All transformer pad locations. Sheet References: Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan)\n\n6. **EL-13.32** - NOT-VERIFIABLE: Cannot confirm drainage slopes away from buildings for oil-filled transformer equipment since equipment type isn't specified on the plans. Code Citation: UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1. Applicable Areas: All transformer locations. Sheet References: Sheet 11 (Grading Plan), Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan)\n\nSeveral earlier items (EL-13.1 through EL-13.9) hinge on site features being present—retaining walls, fences, balconies, stairwells, fire escapes—so I need to verify these actually exist on the site. Items EL-13.12 through EL-13.20 involve clearance distances from various features like fire hydrants, trees, shrubs, dumpsters, bike racks, light poles, fire lanes, and other transformers; I'll need to confirm which of these are present and measure their distances. Gas utility clearances (EL-13.24 through EL-13.25) appear inapplicable since no gas service is mentioned. I should also check for utilities crossing above or below transformers, overhead distribution lines for clearance verification, and niche configuration requirements.\n\nFor property location and easements, the transformers seem to be on private property but I need to confirm this. Bollards aren't needed since the pads sit more than 4 feet from parking areas. I should also verify whether any structures exist over or under overhead distribution lines. Let me cross-reference the fire protection plan to identify any conflicts between the transformer pads and fire lanes or hydrant clearances.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":721,"cache_read_input_tokens":71898,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":721},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64cdee63-31dd-4baa-841a-32fa24fe3ff6","uuid":"40430940-6fdf-4170-9c0e-3f4eadeac21e"}
