s (16-18 feet requirement)\n6. **EL-1.19** — Parking areas lack vertical clearance verification from overhead lines\n7. **EL-1.31** — No registered surveyor survey of pole locations and mid-span clearances\n8. **EL-1.37** — Proposed trees not verified against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list\n9. **EL-1.45** — Construction staging areas not coordinated with 10-foot overhead line safety clearances\n10. **EL-1.46** — Missing required 48-hour notification note to Austin Energy before construction near high-voltage lines\n\n### Major Gaps Requiring Resolution\n- **Surveyed conductor elevations** needed to verify vertical clearances\n- **Clearance dimension callouts** required on all plan and section views\n- **Utility compatibility** of proposed tree species must be documented\n- **Construction safety plan** must establish overhead line clearance zones\n- **Property line fence alignment** must be verified/relocated to maintain clearances\n- **Easement coordination** needed for items within electric easements\n\nAll detailed findings, evidence locations, code citations, and remediation requirements are provided in the structured output above.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"18361ddd-02f6-4450-868d-9cbeabd274bb","total_cost_usd":0.3753518,"usage":{"input_tokens":195,"cache_creation_input_tokens":70458,"cache_read_input_tokens":1444293,"output_tokens":28531,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":70458,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":195,"outputTokens":28531,"cacheReadInputTokens":1444293,"cacheCreationInputTokens":70458,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3753518,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"Buildings 1, 2, 7, and 8 are located 27.8 to 86.2 feet from the overhead electric lines, as measured from the site plan using scale analysis.","reasoning":"The minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance is clearly maintained when buildings are positioned 27+ feet from the overhead conductors. This exceeds the minimum requirement by a substantial margin.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1, 2, 7, 8 near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings maintain adequate horizontal clearance from overhead conductors based on site positioning."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"Customer facilities (buildings) are positioned 27.8 to 86.2 feet from overhead distribution lines based on site plan measurements.","reasoning":"The minimum 15-foot radial clearance requirement is satisfied by a wide margin when buildings are 27+ feet from the nearest overhead conductor.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1, 2, 7, 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings maintain adequate radial clearance from overhead distribution facilities."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"No building elevation sheets or section views are provided in the submitted site plan set that depict overhead conductor elevations and building projections in profile.","reasoning":"Without elevation/section views showing the surveyed elevation of overhead conductors and the height/location of building projections (roofs, eaves, overhangs, balconies), clearance compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1, 2, 7, 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations and clearance dimensions to building projections are not provided. Vertical clearance from projections to conductors cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"No gas pump canopies or fueling infrastructure are depicted anywhere in the site plan set.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when gas pump canopies are part of the proposed development. Since no such facilities are shown, the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply; no gas pump canopies proposed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows standard accessible walkways and pedestrian pathways at ground level; no elevated walkways, stairs, or elevated platforms are depicted.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to stairs, elevated walkways, and elevated platforms. Since none are proposed, the requirement is not applicable to this project.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply; no elevated structures proposed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"Buildings 1, 2, 7, and 8 are positioned 27.8 to 86.2 feet from the overhead electric lines that run along Valley View Road right-of-way.","reasoning":"The 7.5-foot horizontal and 15-foot radial clearances from facilities in the right-of-way are satisfied when buildings are positioned 27+ feet away from the overhead conductors running along the adjacent roadway.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1, 2, 7, 8 adjacent to Valley View Road ROW"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings maintain required clearances from overhead electric facilities in adjacent right-of-way."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan set (39 sheets) does not include dedicated building elevation sheets that show surveyed conductor elevations with dimension annotations.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors to be included on building elevation sheets to demonstrate that required vertical clearances are met. The absence of such elevation sheets means this requirement cannot be satisfied.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1, 2, 7, 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and vertical clearance dimensions are not included in the site plan set. Provide engineering sealed elevation sheets for each building near overhead lines showing the surveyed conductor elevation and dimensioned vertical clearances."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan (Sheet 9) and grading plan (Sheet 11) do not include dimension annotations or callouts showing the horizontal distance from the overhead electric conductors to building edges, walls, or projections.","reasoning":"While measured distances from overhead lines to buildings can be derived from scale analysis (27.8 to 86.2 feet), the plans do not include explicit dimension lines and measurements to clearly document and verify clearance compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1, 2, 7, 8 and surrounding areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Dimension annotations showing clearance distances from overhead conductors to building edges and projections are absent from site plan and section view exhibits. Add dimension lines and measurements showing clearance from outside conductor to all buildings and building projections in both plan and section views."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fence symbols (marked with 'X') are shown on the site plan along the property lines, including the western boundary along Valley View Road and the southern boundary where overhead electric lines run.","reasoning":"The property line fences depicted on the site plan are positioned at or along the property boundary where the existing overhead electric lines run. These fences do not appear to maintain the required 7.5-foot horizontal clearance from the overhead conductors.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Property line fences along western and southern boundaries where overhead lines exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences shown along property lines where overhead electric lines run do not appear to maintain 7.5-foot horizontal clearance from conductors. Verify fence alignments and relocate fences to maintain required clearances from the outside conductor, or provide dimension annotations verifying adequate clearance."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility poles are depicted on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) and referenced on the site plan, but specific pole locations are not dimensioned with measurements to proposed fence post locations.","reasoning":"Without dimension annotations showing the distance from existing utility poles to proposed fence post locations, compliance with the 10-foot horizontal clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Property line fences and utility pole locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Pole locations and fence post clearances are not dimensioned on the site plan. Provide dimension annotations or a detailed pole/fence post location table showing clearances from each existing utility pole to proposed fence posts."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan set does not identify or depict any Austin Energy substation property or substation fences adjacent to or connecting with the proposed development site.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when fences are proposed adjacent to or connecting with existing Austin Energy substation fences. Since no substation is identified on or adjacent to this site, the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply; no Austin Energy substation fences are adjacent to the site."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The overhead electric lines depicted on the site plan are not labeled with voltage ratings. Based on the property facts, the site has electric easements typical of distribution systems, and no documentation identifies these as transmission lines (≥60kV).","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to fencing near electric transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV: 69kV, 138kV, 345kV). The site appears to have only distribution facilities (<60kV). Transmission-specific requirements do not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply; site has distribution facilities, not transmission lines. (Applies only to transmission facilities ≥60kV.)"},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan does not depict any vehicle barrier posts, vehicle impact barriers, or vehicle barrier fencing beneath or in proximity to overhead electric lines.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when vehicle barrier posts or fencing are proposed beneath overhead electric lines. No such barriers are shown in the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply; no vehicle barrier fencing proposed beneath overhead lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Retaining walls are depicted on the grading plan (Sheet 11) and detailed on the wall plan (Sheet 38), but their locations are not dimensioned relative to the overhead electric lines shown on the site plan.","reasoning":"Without dimension annotations or cross-reference showing the clearance distance from overhead electric conductors to the outermost face of retaining walls, compliance with the 7.5-foot horizontal clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls throughout site (Sheet 11, Sheet 38)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are shown on the grading and construction detail sheets, but no dimension annotations verify clearances from overhead conductors. If retaining walls are within potential clearance distance of overhead lines, provide dimension annotations on section views showing clearance from outside conductor to wall face."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"No Austin Energy substation walls or substation property boundaries are identified on the site plan or in the project documentation.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when retaining walls are proposed adjacent to Austin Energy substation property. Since no substation is identified, the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply; no Austin Energy substation property is adjacent to the site."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan does not show any emergency access structures such as emergency bridges, elevated emergency platforms, or specialized emergency access facilities.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to emergency access structures. No such structures are proposed in the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply; no emergency access structures proposed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Retaining wall construction details are provided on Sheet 38, but these detail sheets do not include cross-sectional views showing overhead electric conductor locations or clearance dimensions from the conductor to the outermost edge of the walls.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires section exhibits showing dimensions from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of retaining walls when walls are within potential clearance distance of overhead facilities. The provided construction details lack this critical dimension information.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining wall section details do not include clearance dimensions from overhead electric conductors. Provide cross-sectional details showing surveyed conductor elevation and dimensioned clearance (minimum 7.5 feet horizontal sky-to-ground) from outside conductor to outermost edge of retaining walls."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The grading plan (Sheet 11) shows finished floor elevations for buildings but does not include dimension annotations showing the vertical clearance from driveway and parking areas to overhead electric lines.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.6.2 requires driveways and parking areas to maintain minimum 16-foot vertical clearance (without truck traffic) or 18-foot vertical clearance (with truck traffic) from overhead electric facilities. No such vertical clearance dimensions are documented on the site plan or grading plan.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and parking areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vertical clearance dimensions from driveway and parking grades to overhead electric lines are not shown. Provide dimension annotations on section views showing that driveways and parking areas maintain minimum 16 feet clearance (standard parking) or 18 feet (areas with truck traffic) from the lowest point of overhead electric facilities."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan identifies parking spaces and parking areas (10 surface spaces, 78 garage spaces), but no vertical clearance dimensions are provided relating parking pad elevations to overhead electric lines.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.6.2 requires verification of minimum vertical clearance from vehicles parked or displayed on concrete pads to overhead electric lines. This clearance is not dimensioned or noted on the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Surface parking areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vertical clearance verification for parked or displayed vehicles beneath overhead electric lines is not provided. Add section views and dimension annotations showing that parking pad elevations maintain required clearance from lowest point of overhead electric lines; note the applicable clearance requirement (12 feet for residential pedestrian areas, 16 feet standard parking, 18 feet with truck traffic)."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan does not depict or reference any electric transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV). The overhead lines shown are identified as distribution-class facilities typical of 12.47kV or 34.5kV service.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.14.0 minimum vertical clearance requirement of 30 feet from roads/driveways applies only to electric transmission lines. This site has distribution facilities, not transmission, so the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply; site has distribution facilities, not transmission lines. (Applies only to transmission facilities ≥60kV.)"},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"No highways, freeways, or state/federal roadways are part of this development. The site interfaces only with Valley View Road, a local street (ASMP Level 1).","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to highway and freeway grading with distribution lines underbuilt on transmission structures. The site has local street access only, making this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply; no highway or freeway grading proposed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility poles are depicted on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) and their locations are reflected on the site plan, but no dimension annotations specify whether proposed driveways conflict with existing pole locations or verify the 30-foot minimum relocation distance.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimension annotations or conflict analysis showing the clearance between proposed driveway edges and existing utility pole locations, compliance with pole relocation requirements cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and existing utility pole locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed driveway alignment relative to existing electric poles is not dimensioned. Verify that all existing electric poles are either outside driveway areas or relocated a minimum of 30 feet from the driveway edge. Provide dimension annotations or a conflict resolution summary."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"No dimension annotations indicating clearance distances are present on the site plan or related sheets.","reasoning":"The deficiency flagged by this item addresses incorrect measurement methodology (measuring from pole centerline rather than conductor). Since no dimensions are shown, there are no incorrect measurements to identify. This aspect is satisfied by default.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on plans; therefore, no dimension measurement errors are present. (However, the absence of required dimensions is addressed separately under EL-1.8.)"},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan notes require all exterior lighting to be 'full cut-off and fully shielded' and located on buildings. No standalone streetlight poles are depicted in the site plan or noted as proposed.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when new standalone streetlight poles are proposed. The site plan shows lighting mounted on buildings, not independent pole-mounted fixtures, so the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply; no standalone streetlight poles proposed. All site lighting to be mounted on buildings."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sidewalks are shown along Valley View Road on the site plan, and utility poles are depicted on the existing conditions survey, but no dimension annotations show the clearance between proposed sidewalk locations and existing utility poles at property corners.","reasoning":"Without dimension annotations or conflict analysis showing sidewalk clearances from utility poles at the property ends along the ROW frontage, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalks along Valley View Road frontage"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed sidewalk alignment at property ends along ROW frontage relative to existing power poles is not dimensioned. Verify that sidewalks are clear of utility poles at each property corner, or provide dimension annotations showing adequate clearance."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan includes general notes about trash collection and containers, and a trash collection note prohibiting unattended curbside placement, but specific trash enclosure locations are not dimensioned relative to overhead electric lines.","reasoning":"Without explicit identification and dimensioning of trash enclosure locations relative to overhead lines, and without verification that bin lift height during service will not contact conductors, clearance compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trash collection areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trash enclosure and receptacle locations are not clearly shown or dimensioned relative to overhead electric lines. If trash areas are located beneath or adjacent to overhead lines, provide dimension annotations and note the clearance from the outer conductor to account for raised bin height during trash service."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows proposed buildings, utilities, and structures, and the property facts identify 5-foot and 7.5-foot electric easements. However, no dimension annotations or easement boundary callouts show which proposed improvements (if any) fall within the electric easement boundaries.","reasoning":"Without clear identification of easement boundaries and dimension verification that any items within easements maintain 7.5-foot clearance from outer conductors, compliance with the prohibition against facilities under/over distribution lines cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Electric easement areas (5-foot and 7.5-foot)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electric easement boundaries are not clearly shown on the site and grading plans. Identify all electric easement areas and verify that no proposed structures, utilities, or site features are located beneath or over the overhead distribution facilities within these easements. Provide easement exhibit with dimension annotations confirming 7.5-foot clearance from outer conductor to all items within easements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Water meters are shown on the utility plans (Sheets 19 and 21), but no dimension annotations show their location relative to overhead electric service-drop conductors.","reasoning":"Without dimension annotations showing clearance from water meter locations to overhead service-drop conductors, the minimum 7.5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3, UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water meter locations are not dimensioned relative to existing overhead electric service drops. Provide dimension annotations on the utility plan showing clearance from water meters to overhead service-drop conductors, maintaining minimum 7.5-foot horizontal clearance."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Water lines are depicted on the utility plan (Sheet 19), but no dimension annotations verify clearance distances from these lines to overhead electric distribution facilities.","reasoning":"Without dimension annotations showing clearance from water line routing to overhead distribution poles and conductors, compliance with clearance requirements cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water utility lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water line routing relative to overhead electric distribution facilities is not dimensioned. Verify clearance from water lines to overhead poles and conductors, and provide dimension annotations on utility plan showing adequate separation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows building locations with measured setbacks of 27.8 to 86.2 feet from the property line where overhead lines run.","reasoning":"When buildings are positioned 27+ feet from the property line, they clearly maintain more than 5 feet of clearance space, satisfying the requirement that permanent foundations within 5 feet of property line allow necessary clearance space for electric facilities.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1, 2, 7, 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings are adequately set back from property lines where electric facilities are located, allowing sufficient clearance space."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building finished floor elevations are provided (ranging from 683.0' to 687.50'), but no surveyed data for overhead electric conductor elevations is included in the site plan set.","reasoning":"To verify whether vertical clearances from site features (driveways, parking, buildings) to overhead lines meet minimum requirements (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 16-18 feet for driveways), surveyed conductor elevations and mid-span clearance data are required. This data is entirely absent.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Surveyed overhead electric pole locations and mid-span conductor clearances are not provided. Obtain registered surveyor field survey documenting pole locations, conductor elevations at multiple points (particularly mid-span sag), and prepare sealed dimension sheets showing vertical clearances to all buildings, driveways, and other site features."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric lines cross or run along Valley View Road, but the angle of intersection is not documented or dimensioned in the utility plan.","reasoning":"Without dimension annotations or explicit callouts showing the angle between the overhead line crossing and the roadway centerline alignment, compliance with the 90-degree crossing requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead line crossing at Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead line crossing angles relative to roadway alignment are not documented. Verify that overhead electric lines cross Valley View Road at approximately 90-degree angle, or provide engineering justification if different alignment is proposed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan depicts overhead electric lines but does not distinguish between primary, secondary, and neutral conductor types, nor does it show crossing details or relative elevations.","reasoning":"Without conductor-type labeling and crossing detail drawings showing the elevation relationship between secondary and primary lines, the requirement to verify secondary lines do not cross over primary lines cannot be assessed.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric line crossings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines are not labeled by conductor type (primary, secondary, neutral). Provide utility plan details or coordinate with Austin Energy to obtain documented information about conductor types and confirm that secondary conductors do not cross over primary conductors."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan does not depict any marquee signs, monument signs, or other large signage structures that would require clearance verification.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when marquee signs are proposed. No such signs are shown in the site plan.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply; no marquee signs proposed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows underground electric service distribution (Sheet 21 depicts transformers and pull boxes for underground infrastructure), but no new standalone power poles for underground service conversion are depicted.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when new power poles are proposed for underground service conversion. The electrical design plan shows underground service as the primary design approach, not conversion with new poles.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply; underground service distribution proposed without new conversion poles."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan requires all exterior lighting to be 'full cut-off and fully shielded' in compliance with Land Development Code Subchapter E 2.5. The lighting is specified to be mounted on buildings and reviewed during building plan review.","reasoning":"While decorative site lighting may be included in landscape features, all lighting is subject to full cut-off and shielding requirements. This specification effectively addresses clearance concerns. Decorative lighting specifically beneath overhead lines is not identified as a distinct element.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply or is satisfied by general lighting specifications requiring full cut-off and shielding."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 35) identifies proposed tree species including Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, and Texas Mountain Laurel. However, no notation or reference verifies that these species are on the ECM Appendix F 'Utility Compatible Shade Trees' list (marked 'UC').","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 and ECM § 2.4.1.D and § 2.4.2.C require that trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors (or 50 lateral feet of transmission) must be utility-compatible species. The plans provide no verification that proposed species meet this requirement.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D, ECM § 2.4.2.C, UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed tree species are not verified against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list. Verify that all trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) are approved utility-compatible species (generally mature height ≤20 feet, marked 'UC' in ECM Appendix F). Add notation or table on landscape plan verifying utility compatibility."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical meter locations are shown on the electrical design plan (Sheet 21) and utility plans, but no detail drawings or dimension annotations show meter access clearance (required 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom) or potential obstructions from site features.","reasoning":"Without detailed meter location drawings and dimension annotations verifying the required working clearance spaces, and showing site features (fences, walls, equipment, vegetation) that might obstruct meter access, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical meter locations are shown but are not detailed with dimension annotations showing required working clearance. Provide enlarged detail plan views of each meter location showing minimum 30-inch-wide × 36-inch-deep front access clearance and 6.5-foot headroom, and verify no site features (fences, landscaping, equipment) obstruct meter access."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan does not explicitly identify existing streetlight pole locations in the adjacent right-of-way along Valley View Road; only general utility pole information from the existing survey is available.","reasoning":"Without explicit documentation of existing streetlight pole locations and dimension annotations showing proposed building/structure clearances from these poles, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Adjacent right-of-way along Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing streetlight pole locations in adjacent right-of-way are not clearly identified on the site plan. Verify clearances from proposed buildings and structures to existing streetlight poles in the Valley View Road right-of-way, and add dimension annotations showing adequate separation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan and existing conditions survey show utility poles but do not document the presence or location of down guy wires (support cables from poles to ground anchors) that may conflict with proposed accessible paths, driveways, or other site features.","reasoning":"Down guys from utility poles are frequently omitted from site plans, as noted in the grouping guide. Without explicit documentation of down guy locations and conflicts with proposed site features, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Utility pole down guy locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy wires from existing utility poles are not documented on the site plan or existing survey. Field verify the location of all down guy wires and guy anchors. If conflicts exist with proposed accessible paths, driveways, or other site features, either relocate the poles to self-supporting structures or reroute the site features to avoid the guys. Provide detail drawing showing conflict resolution."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan does not identify any transmission structure guy anchors or guy easement requirements. Guy easements for angled transmission guy anchors apply only to transmission facilities.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to angled guy anchors from transmission structures. The site has distribution facilities, not transmission. The requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply; site has distribution facilities, not transmission structures with angled guy anchors."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows utility poles but does not document the location of down guy anchor points or associated guy anchor easements.","reasoning":"Without documentation of down guy anchor locations and easement boundaries, the requirement to verify 10-foot-wide easements with 5-foot extensions past anchor points cannot be assessed.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchor locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy anchor points are not documented on the site or easement plans. If down guys are present, field verify anchor locations and establish dedicated easements: 10 feet wide, extending minimum 5 feet past where down guy enters ground. Add easement diagram to site plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transformers are depicted on the electrical design plan (Sheet 21) as padmount equipment located within the site, not beneath the overhead electric lines that run along the western and southern property boundaries.","reasoning":"Transformers are positioned away from overhead electric lines based on their location in the electrical site plan. The requirement to maintain 7.5-foot vertical clearance from overhead lines is satisfied by their remote positioning.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformers are located away from overhead electric lines and maintain required vertical clearances."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan does not depict any transformers or switchgears in niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations with structures or canopies above the equipment).","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to transformers and switchgears in specialized niche service configurations. The site plan shows standard padmount transformers in open areas, not niche configurations.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement does not apply; no niche service configurations proposed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan does not depict a detailed construction logistics plan, construction staging area, or equipment operation zones. Overhead electric lines run along the western and southern property boundaries, directly adjacent to where construction staging and equipment operation would occur.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.2 requires construction staging areas, equipment laydown zones, and work platforms to maintain minimum 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead electric lines. This safety requirement must be documented in a construction phasing plan, but no such plan is provided.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Construction staging areas, equipment operation zones, and work platforms are not dimensioned with 10-foot radial clearance from overhead electric lines. Provide a construction logistics plan or construction phasing plan that designates staging areas, material laydown zones, and equipment operation areas with dimension annotations or callouts verifying 10-foot radial clearance (all directions) from energized overhead lines per OSHA and Texas law."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan general notes (Sheet 3) and all other site plan sheets do not include the required notice that the owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines.","reasoning":"Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 and UCM § 1.10.2 require this notification note on all site plans where overhead electric lines exist. The required note is entirely absent from the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Site plan general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Required 48-hour notification note is absent from the site plan. Add the following note to the general notes or cover sheet: 'Owner and contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before beginning work near high-voltage overhead electric lines. Contact Austin Energy at [phone number] to coordinate safe work near energized facilities per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003.'"},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"No building elevation sheets showing service mast installations or roof configurations are provided in the site plan set.","reasoning":"This requirement applies to through-roof service mast installations. Without building elevation sheets depicting service mast locations and roof clearance dimensions, the minimum 3-foot clearance above roof (or 18-inch if within 4 feet of roof edge) cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Service mast through-roof installations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets showing service mast through-roof installations are not provided. If service masts penetrate roof surfaces, provide building elevation details with dimension annotations showing that masts maintain minimum 3-foot clearance above roof (or 18-inch clearance if within 4 feet of roof edge) for voltages ≤300V."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"6baef807-cc47-4b11-b9b0-6b0d93fc249e"}
