uilding floor plans. No external stairwells are positioned adjacent to any transformer pad.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (stairwells adjacent to transformer) is not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Reviewed fire protection plan (Sheet 10) and site plan. No fire escapes or exterior stairs serving as fire escapes are located near transformer pads.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (fire escapes/stairs present) is not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pad locations on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad access door locations and orientations are not marked or labeled on the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan. Without access door orientation, the 10-foot hot-stick clearance requirement cannot be verified for each specific pad.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision examination of Sheet 21 shows transformer pads depicted as square symbols with circles inside and leader lines to labels reading 'Electrical Transformer Pad.' No arrows, door labels, or directional indicators mark access door sides.","reasoning":"The code requires 10-foot clearance specifically from the access door side. Without documented access door orientation on the plans, compliance with this directional requirement cannot be verified. This is a preliminary design, but access door orientation is critical for clearance verification.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],