erground utilities shown on the Utility Tap Plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan shows water, wastewater, and storm drain routing. Transformer locations are positioned to avoid conflicts with utility infrastructure.","reasoning":"While some water line clearances are inadequate (EL-13.21), the 12-inch minimum clearance from other utilities (beyond water, wastewater, and storm that are specifically governed by other sections) appears to be maintained.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad and utility locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans show no transformer pads or Austin Energy facilities located over or under other utility lines. No customer buildings or structures are installed over AE underground facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Reviewed electrical plan (Sheet 21) and utility plan (Sheet 19). Transformer pads are positioned in surface areas with no indication of stacking or crossing conflicts with utilities.","reasoning":"The plan layout shows separation of electrical and other utility infrastructure. No crossing conflicts are evident.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to overhead distribution lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution lines are shown on the site plan. Transformer pads are supplied by underground service. The 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) show underground electrical service routing with no overhead distribution infrastructure.","reasoning":"Without overhead distribution lines present, the vertical clearance requirement is not applicable to transformer pad locations.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to overhead distribution"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors are shown on the site plan. Service is provided via underground lines. The 15-foot radius clearance requirement from overhead conductors does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical and utility plans show underground distribution service. No overhead conductors are visible on any sheet.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (overhead distribution conductors present) is not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not located in niches (enclosed areas within building footprints accessible from outside). All transformers are pad-mounted in surface locations. Niche vertical clearance requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site and electrical plans show transformer pads positioned in open site areas outside building footprints.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (transformer located in niche with building footprint) is not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Niche service installation is not proposed. Transformers are standard pad-mounted equipment outside building footprints. Fire wall and ventilation requirements for niche installations do not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plans show transformer pads as surface-mounted equipment in site areas, not within building envelopes.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (niche service proposed) is not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (survey requirement as required by AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad access areas where overhead structures or enclosed areas may exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances in access paths to transformer pads. While overhead structures do not appear to be present, cross-sections demonstrating clearance compliance would be required if any overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas existed above transformer locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan set reviewed for cross-section drawings. No cross-sections specifically showing vertical clearances to transformer pads were found.","reasoning":"While the site layout suggests overhead structures are not present above transformer pads, AE Design standards may require cross-section documentation. This documentation is not provided and cannot be verified as present or adequate.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations where oil-filled equipment may be installed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical specifications do not identify whether proposed transformers are oil-filled or dry-type equipment. Grading plan does not show explicit drainage direction notation around transformer pad locations. Without equipment type specification and detailed grading notation, compliance with the requirement that liquid flow must be away from buildings cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan sheet shows transformer pad locations but does not specify equipment type. Grading plan shows contours and general drainage patterns but does not provide specific notation of flow direction around transformer pads.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment due to fire risk from insulating oil. Without equipment type identified and without explicit grading notation showing drainage direction, this requirement cannot be verified as applicable or compliant.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are located within the subject property boundaries (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision) shown on the site plan. No transformer pads are straddling property lines or located in the public right-of-way.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows property boundaries and transformer pad locations. All pads are positioned within the lot boundaries in private areas.","reasoning":"Transformer pads are clearly within private property boundaries per the plat and site plan layout.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4 (property requirement); easement-specific regulations"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to easements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple existing easements are recorded on the property (drainage, wastewater, electrical, public utility) per facts.md