{"level":30,"time":1778523906746,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JYskxk6w7CHsiFBz2U4oxN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I've completed the structured output with all 39 checklist items evaluated. The key findings are:\n\nFAILS (2 items):\n1. EL-13.21 - Three transformer pads violate 5-foot water line clearance\n2. EL-13.22 - One transformer pad violates 5-foot wastewater clearance\n\nNOT-VERIFIABLE (5 items):\n1. EL-13.10 - Hot-stick access door orientations not marked\n2. EL-13.34 - Transformer pads relative to existing easements not clearly documented\n3. EL-13.35 - Transformer easements not shown (noted as future requirement)\n4. EL-13.36 - Electrical routing to private property not explicitly verified\n5. EL-13.37 - Transformer pad dimensions not matching AE Design details\n\nThese findings are significant because:\n- The water line and wastewater line violations are direct code compliance failures\n- The lack of access door marking makes hot-stick clearance verification impossible\n- Missing transformer easements and pad dimension details suggest incomplete design coordination with Austin Energy\n\nThe review shows that the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan is incomplete in several respects and will require coordination with Austin Energy Design for finalized transformer specifications and easement documentation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12140,"cache_read_input_tokens":75562,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12140},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64cdee63-31dd-4baa-841a-32fa24fe3ff6","uu