{"level":30,"time":1778523906746,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JYskxk6w7CHsiFBz2U4oxN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the comprehensive review of Grouping 13 (Transformer Pad Clearances and Location Requirements) for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nI evaluated all 39 checklist items and identified:\n\n### **Critical Failures (2 items):**\n1. **EL-13.21 - Water Line Clearances**: Three transformer pads lack the required 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from water service lines:\n   - Pad west of Building 2: 1.4 feet (violates by 3.6 feet)\n   - Pad west of Building 8: 3.7 feet (violates by 1.3 feet)  \n   - Pad east of Building 6: 3.5 feet (violates by 1.5 feet)\n\n2. **EL-13.22 - Wastewater Line Clearance**: One transformer pad lacks the required 5-foot minimum clearance from wastewater lines:\n   - Pad west of Building 1: 4.9 feet (violates by 0.1 foot)\n\n### **Cannot Be Verified (5 items):**\n1. **EL-13.10** - Hot-stick access door side clearances cannot be verified because access door orientations are not marked on the electrical plan\n2. **EL-13.34** - Cannot verify transformer pads are not in prohibited easements; existing recorded easements are not clearly depicted relative to transformer locations\n3. **EL-13.35** - Transformer easements are not shown on the site plan; general notes indicate they may be required at a later date\n4. **EL-13.36** - Electrical routing from transformers to meters not verified as 100% on private property\n5. **EL-13.37** - Transformer pad dimensions not shown and do not reference Austin Energy Design-approved detail sheets\n\n### **Passes (17 items):**\nClearances adequately maintained for buildings, storm drains, fire lanes, bollard separation, and other site features where applicable.\n\n### **Not Applicable (17 items):**\nConditions triggering these requirements (retaining walls, fences, fire escapes, niche configurations, gas service, overhead lines, etc.) are either not present or do not apply to this project.\n\nThe Preliminary Electrical Design Plan requires coordination with Austin Energy Design to finalize transformer specifications, establish easements, and mark access door orientations."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12140,"cache_read_input_tokens":75562,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12140},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64cdee63-31dd-4baa-841a-32fa24fe3ff6","uuid":"15db4c53-9c7f-4e52-8606-8ab6da28e519"}
