.7 feet clearance, which satisfies the standard.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No retaining walls shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Reviewed site plan sheets showing building layout, grading plan, and electrical plan. No retaining walls are positioned adjacent to any transformer pad.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (retaining walls present and adjacent to pads) is not met. This item is not applicable to this project.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences are shown on the site plan but are not located immediately adjacent to transformer pads. Measured clearances to fenced areas are well beyond 3-5 foot minimums required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Examined site plan and electrical plan to identify fence locations relative to transformer pads. Fences exist on site but are not positioned directly adjacent to any transformer pad.","reasoning":"While fences are present on the site, they do not appear to be located at the minimum clearance distances from any transformer pad, suggesting adequate separation or that the applicability condition is not triggered.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearances less than 5 feet to buildings are shown or documented as intentional design features requiring reduced clearance exception.","agentTrace":{"observation":"All measured transformer pad clearances from buildings are 6.7 feet or greater, exceeding the 5-foot minimum by at least 1.7 feet.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (clearances shown as less than 5 feet) is not met. No reduced clearances are documented, so this exception requirement is not triggered.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No balconies or overhangs are shown directly above or adjacent to transformer pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Reviewed building elevation and site plan sheets. Transformer pads are located in open areas without overhead structures.","reasoning":"No building features (balconies, overhangs, covered areas) are positioned directly above or immediately adjacent to any transformer pad. Applicability condition not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on plans, making applicability indeterminate. For dry-type equipment, this requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan sheets do not specify whether proposed transformers are oil-filled or dry-type equipment.","reasoning":"The requirement only applies to oil-filled equipment with windows/doors/ventilating ducts at inadequate separation. Without equipment type specification, this cannot be confirmed as applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No public sidewalks are located adjacent to transformer pads. Transformer pads are in internal site areas with adequate clearance from any back of sidewalk.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Reviewed site plan showing site perimeter and internal layout. No sidewalks are shown immediately adjacent to transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (sidewalks adjacent to pads) is not met. Transformer pads are in internal site areas, not at property boundaries with adjacent sidewalks.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairwells are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Reviewed site plan and building floor plans. No external stairwells are positioned adjacent to any transformer pad.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (stairwells adjacent to transformer) is not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Reviewed fire protection plan (Sheet 10) and site plan. No fire escapes or exterior stairs serving as fire escapes are located near transformer pads.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (fire escapes/stairs present) is not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pad locations on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad access door locations and orientations are not marked or labeled on the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan. Without access door orientation, the 10-foot hot-stick clearance requirement cannot be verified for each specific pad.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision examination of Sheet 21 shows transformer pads depicted as square symbols with circles inside and leader lines to labels reading 'Electrical Transformer Pad.' No arrows, door labels, or directional indicators mark access door sides.","reasoning":"The code requires 10-foot clearance specifically from the access door side. Without documented access door orientation on the plans, compliance with this directional requirement cannot be verified. This is a preliminary design, but access door orientation is critical for clearance verification.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations if any face confined spaces"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer pads are clearly documented as facing confined spaces (niches, vaults, enclosed areas on 3+ sides). Additionally, access door orientations are not marked, making determination of confined space facing impossible. The 15-foot clearance requirement for confined space facing cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows transformer pads in general site areas. No cross-section drawings or architectural details indicate any pads are located in niches or facing enclosed areas. Access door markings (needed to determine which direction is 'facing') are absent.","reasoning":"Confined space applicability requires both that a niche/enclosed area exists AND that the access door faces it. Without either documentation or access door orientation marking, this requirement cannot be verified as applicable or compliant.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Site with private fire hydrant"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"One private fire hydrant is shown on the site plan (Sheet 10). Transformer pad locations are at adequate distance (well beyond 5 feet) from the hydrant location.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire Protection Plan shows one private fire hydrant on the site. Transformer pad locations are in separate areas of the development.","reasoning":"The visible spatial separation between hydrant and transformer pad locations exceeds the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas near transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are not labeled or referenced on the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31). Trees shown on the landscape plan are identified only by symbols (SY, PL, P, M) without species names. Cross-reference to tree list (Sheet 32) required to verify utility-compatible species per ECM Appendix F.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows trees with symbol designations but no species names. Transformer pads are not marked/labeled on landscape sheet, preventing proximity analysis. Tree species and utility compatibility information is not on Sheet 31.","reasoning":"Without tree species identification linked to transformer locations, and with transformer pad locations not marked on the landscape sheet, utility compatibility cannot be verified. The plant schedule/tree list required for this verification is on a different sheet not yet cross-referenced.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas near transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are not marked or labeled on the Landscape Plan, preventing verification of shrub/vegetation clearances from transformer access door sides.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows various plantings but transformer pads are not identified or marked with access door orientation.","reasoning":"Without transformer pad locations and access door orientation marked on the landscape plan, and without access door orientation specified anywhere on the electrical plan, the required 10-foot clearance from access door side and 5-foot clearance from other sides cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas near transformer locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations not marked on landscape plan. Root barrier details not provided for any trees that may be within 20 lateral feet of transformer locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan does not identify transformer pad locations or reference any root barrier details near electrical infrastructure.","reasoning":"Without transformer locations marked on landscape sheets and without root barrier specifications shown, this requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Dumpster enclosure areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Dumpster enclosures shown on site plan are not located adjacent to transformer pad areas. Adequate clearance (well beyond 5 feet) is maintained.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows dumpster locations in separate areas from transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"The spatial separation between dumpster enclosures and transformer pads exceeds the 5-foot minimum requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Bicycle parking areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Bicycle parking facilities are shown on the site plan but are located at adequate distance from transformer pad locations, exceeding the 5-foot minimum clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows bicycle parking in building areas. Transformer pads are in separate utility areas of the site.","reasoning":"Spatial separation between bicycle parking facilities and transformer pads exceeds the 5-foot minimum.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Light pole and transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Light pole locations not clearly marked on site plan in relation to transformer pad locations. Cannot verify 5-foot clearance without labeled light pole positions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and landscape plan show site layout but light pole positions are not explicitly cross-referenced with transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Without explicit identification of light pole locations relative to transformer pads, the 5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fire lanes on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire lanes are designated on the Fire Protection Plan. Transformer pad locations maintain adequate clearance from fire lanes, exceeding the 15-foot minimum separation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire Protection Plan shows fire lane routing. Transformer pad locations are positioned in utility service areas away from fire circulation routes.","reasoning":"The spatial separation between transformer pads and designated fire lanes exceeds the 15-foot minimum requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations where multiple pads exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Five transformer pads are shown on the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan. Measured distances between individual transformer pads exceed 5-foot minimum separation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows five distinct transformer pad locations. Measured separations between pads range from approximately 15 feet to over 70 feet.","reasoning":"All transformer-to-transformer separations exceed the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad west of Building 2","Transformer pad west of Building 8","Transformer pad east of Building 6"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Three transformer pads lack the required minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from proposed water service lines: pad west of Building 2 (1.4 feet), pad west of Building 8 (3.7 feet), and pad east of Building 6 (3.5 feet). All are significantly below the 5-foot minimum requirement per UCM Section 2.9.1.B.2.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 19) shows water line routing and transformer pad locations. Measurements from pad edges to nearest blue water service lines yielded: 1.4 feet, 3.7 feet, and 3.5 feet for three pads.","reasoning":"The measured clearances are less than the 5-foot horizontal minimum required by the code. This is a direct and measurable code violation for three transformer pads.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad west of Building 1"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad west of Building 1 has a 4.9-foot horizontal clearance from the proposed wastewater line, which is less than the 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance required per UCM Section 2.9.1.B.2.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of Utility Tap Plan shows wastewater line (purple/magenta line) proximity to transformer pad west of Building 1, measuring 4.9 feet from pad edge to line.","reasoning":"The measured clearance of 4.9 feet is below the 5-foot horizontal minimum required by code. This represents a 0.1-foot violation of the standard.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from storm drain lines. Measured clearances range from 8.5 feet to 59.3 feet, all exceeding the 5-foot minimum.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of Utility Tap Plan shows storm drain line locations and distances to all five transformer pads: 59.1 feet, 51.5 feet, 8.5 feet, 59.3 feet, and 52.1 feet respectively.","reasoning":"All measured clearances exceed the 5-foot horizontal minimum requirement per UCM Section 2.9.1.B.2.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas service is shown or identified on the site plan or utility plans. Gas clearance requirements do not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Reviewed facts.md and all utility plan sheets. No gas service, gas lines, or gas infrastructure are mentioned or depicted.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (gas service present on site) is not met. This requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads maintain minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearance from other underground utilities shown on the Utility Tap Plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan shows water, wastewater, and storm drain routing. Transformer locations are positioned to avoid conflicts with utility infrastructure.","reasoning":"While some water line clearances are inadequate (EL-13.21), the 12-inch minimum clearance from other utilities (beyond water, wastewater, and storm that are specifically governed by other sections) appears to be maintained.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad and utility locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans show no transformer pads or Austin Energy facilities located over or under other utility lines. No customer buildings or structures are installed over AE underground facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Reviewed electrical plan (Sheet 21) and utility plan (Sheet 19). Transformer pads are positioned in surface areas with no indication of stacking or crossing conflicts with utilities.","reasoning":"The plan layout shows separation of electrical and other utility infrastructure. No crossing conflicts are evident.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to overhead distribution lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution lines are shown on the site plan. Transformer pads are supplied by underground service. The 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) show underground electrical service routing with no overhead distribution infrastructure.","reasoning":"Without overhead distribution lines present, the vertical clearance requirement is not applicable to transformer pad locations.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to overhead distribution"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors are shown on the site plan. Service is provided via underground lines. The 15-foot radius clearance requirement from overhead conductors does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical and utility plans show underground distribution service. No overhead conductors are visible on any sheet.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (overhead distribution conductors present) is not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not located in niches (enclosed areas within building footprints accessible from outside). All transformers are pad-mounted in surface locations. Niche vertical clearance requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site and electrical plans show transformer pads positioned in open site areas outside building footprints.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (transformer located in niche with building footprint) is not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Niche service installation is not proposed. Transformers are standard pad-mounted equipment outside building footprints. Fire wall and ventilation requirements for niche installations do not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plans show transformer pads as surface-mounted equipment in site areas, not within building envelopes.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (niche service proposed) is not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (survey requirement as required by AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad access areas where overhead structures or enclosed areas may exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances in access paths to transformer pads. While overhead structures do not appear to be present, cross-sections demonstrating clearance compliance would be required if any overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas existed above transformer locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan set reviewed for cross-section drawings. No cross-sections specifically showing vertical clearances to transformer pads were found.","reasoning":"While the site layout suggests overhead structures are not present above transformer pads, AE Design standards may require cross-section documentation. This documentation is not provided and cannot be verified as present or adequate.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations where oil-filled equipment may be installed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical specifications do not identify whether proposed transformers are oil-filled or dry-type equipment. Grading plan does not show explicit drainage direction notation around transformer pad locations. Without equipment type specification and detailed grading notation, compliance with the requirement that liquid flow must be away from buildings cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan sheet shows transformer pad locations but does not specify equipment type. Grading plan shows contours and general drainage patterns but does not provide specific notation of flow direction around transformer pads.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment due to fire risk from insulating oil. Without equipment type identified and without explicit grading notation showing drainage direction, this requirement cannot be verified as applicable or compliant.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are located within the subject property boundaries (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision) shown on the site plan. No transformer pads are straddling property lines or located in the public right-of-way.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows property boundaries and transformer pad locations. All pads are positioned within the lot boundaries in private areas.","reasoning":"Transformer pads are clearly within private property boundaries per the plat and site plan layout.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4 (property requirement); easement-specific regulations"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to easements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple existing easements are recorded on the property (drainage, wastewater, electrical, public utility) per facts.md. Transformer pad locations relative to these easements cannot be fully verified. Some transformer pads may be located within or adjacent to existing drainage or utility easements without documented Austin Energy Design written approval.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md documents multiple recorded easements: drainage easement (NE corner), wastewater easement (10-foot width), electrical easements (5-foot width, x2), public utility easement (7.5-foot). These easements are not clearly depicted or referenced on current site plan sheets relative to transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Without clear identification of easement boundaries relative to transformer pad locations, and without documented AE Design written approval for placement within prohibited easements, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (additional clearance and access easements may be required)"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements are not shown on the site plan sheets. General notes on Sheet 3 state 'Additional electric easements may be required at a later date,' indicating easements have not been finalized. Easement boundaries and widths required for Austin Energy accessibility cannot be verified as adequate or shown on submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Reviewed plat (Sheet 2), site plan (Sheet 9), electrical plan (Sheet 21), and general notes (Sheet 3). No separate easement exhibit shows transformer access easements. Sheet 3 Release Notes, item 5, states 'Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.'","reasoning":"Transformer easements are required per UCM but are not shown on the submitted plans. The general note indicates they have not been finalized, suggesting they are outstanding items for design coordination.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical routing from transformer to meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical routing from proposed transformer pads to meter locations is shown on the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan but routing paths are not clearly marked or verified as 100% on private property. Routing across property boundaries or near property lines cannot be excluded without explicit labeling.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows transformer and meter locations with connecting electrical lines but does not explicitly label which portions are on private vs. public property.","reasoning":"Without explicit property boundary notation or labels confirming electrical routing is entirely on private property, this requirement cannot be definitively verified as compliant.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0 (obtain transformer pad detail from AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions (length, width, height) are not provided on the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan. Plans do not reference or include Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets that specify exact dimensions for the proposed service type (single-phase or three-phase). Pad dimensions cannot be verified as matching AE Design standards.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations with symbols but no dimension callouts or reference to detail sheets. No AE Design-approved pad details are included in the submitted plan set.","reasoning":"The grouping explicitly states pad dimensions are determined by AE Design on a project-specific basis and are not standardized. The absence of dimension callouts and AE Design detail references means compliance cannot be verified. This is likely a preliminary design issue to be resolved during detailed design/permitting.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to parking areas and vehicle circulation"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads are located more than 4 feet from parking areas and vehicle circulation routes. Measured distances range from 16 feet to 85.3 feet. Since no pads are within the 4-foot trigger distance, bollards are not required per this standard.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Measured distances from all transformer pads to nearest parking or traffic areas: 32.2 feet, 16 feet, 31.2 feet, 74.4 feet, and 85.3 feet.","reasoning":"All clearances exceed the 4-foot threshold that triggers bollard requirement. Bollards are not required where pads are adequately separated from traffic areas.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building and site structure locations relative to overhead distribution"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution facilities are shown on site. All electrical service is provided via underground lines. No customer buildings, parking garages, light poles, signs, billboards, chimneys, antennas, or tanks are installed under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and electrical plan show no overhead distribution infrastructure on the property.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (overhead distribution facilities present) is not met.","tools_used":[]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"51388f7c-2eb9-46dd-a967-daa9fa3085a6"}
