{"level":30,"time":1778523945882,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ErgRrALLsuTnKe9aHqQAvy","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21), here is the information regarding the electric equipment. \n\n**Important Note:** The requested Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) showing *proposed* tree locations was not provided in the image. Therefore, I cannot describe the equipment's location relative to the proposed trees. However, I can describe its location relative to the buildings and the *existing* tree canopies (indicated by the large, wavy circular outlines) shown on this sheet.\n\n### Underground/Site Electric Equipment Shown:\nThe electrical infrastructure is designated primarily by blue lines and boxes with corresponding labels. The following equipment is explicitly labeled on the plan:\n\n**1. \"Underground Electric Line\"**\n*   Represented by the network of solid blue lines routing throughout the site. \n*   Specific labels for \"Underground Electric Line\" point to the blue line running north-south along the western edge (inside the \"Sidewalk Easement\") and the line running east-west between Bldg 4 and Bldg 7.\n\n**2. \"Electrical Pull Box\"**\nThese are represented by small blue squares along the underground electric lines. They are located in the following areas:\n*   Near the main western site boundary, inside the \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n*   West of Bldg 1 (near the transformer pad).\n*   West of Bldg 2 (near the transformer pad).\n*   West of Bldg 8 (near the \"Vault Easement\").\n*   Northwest corner of Bldg 4 (between Bldg 3 and 4).\n*   South of Bldg 4 / North of Bldg 7.\n*   East of Bldg 7 (near the transformer pad).\n*   South of Bldg 6, near the southern property line boundary.\n\n**3. \"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**\nThese are represented by blue rectangles. (Note: The label specifies \"Pad,\" which typically indicates surface-mounted equipment rather than buried, but they are part of the underground routing system). They are located:\n*   West side of Bldg 1.\n*   West side of Bldg 2.\n*   West side of Bldg 8.\n*   East side of Bldg 5.\n*   South side of Bldg 7.\n\n**4. \"Vault Easement\"**\n*   A designated \"Vault Easement\" is labeled on the western side of the property, directly west of Bldg 8, adjacent to an \"Electrical Pull Box\" and \"Electrical Meters.\" \n\n**5. \"Electrical Meters\"**\n*   Meter banks (represented by small adjoining blue squares) are labeled on the exterior walls of all buildings (Bldgs 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, and 8).\n\n### Location Relative to Trees Visible on Sheet 21:\nWhile proposed trees from Sheet 31 are not visible, Sheet 21 depicts numerous *existing* trees using large, faint, wavy circular outlines. \n*   The **\"Underground Electric Line\"** network directly intersects and routes through the canopies of multiple existing trees, particularly along the northern property line above Bldgs 1 and 3, along the western sidewalk easement next to Bldgs 2 and 8, and along the eastern and southern edges of the site.\n*   Several **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** locations and **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** locations appear to sit within or directly on the edge of these existing tree canopy outlines."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dedcba6e-469f-4ff1-8623-d3aaae962125","uuid":"4f072e6c-bf9f-4de7-a84e-98ce7422d6ae","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21), here is the information regarding the electric equipment. \n\n**Important Note:** The requested Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) showing *proposed* tree locations was not provided in the image. Therefore, I cannot describe the equipment's location relative to the proposed trees. However, I can describe its location relative to the building