{"level":30,"time":1778524284694,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019qbFymRJbTb9wgvVQgEQdW","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Electric Review\n     2→\n     3→*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n     4→\n     5→Electric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n     6→\n     7→See Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\n     8→Link: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\n     9→Applicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n    10→\n    11→Site Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\n    12→Austin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n    13→* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n    14→* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n    15→* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n    16→* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n    17→* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n    18→* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n    19→* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n    20→* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n    21→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dedcba6e-469f-4ff1-8623-d3aaae962125","uuid":"882ace31-e83f-4afb-8df9-53632149f55f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md","content":"# Electric Review\n\n*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n\nElectric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n\nSee Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\nLink: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\nApplicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n\nSite Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\nAustin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778524284694,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WCN97REZQEnpBsFSimnm8E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! The Electric Review section references:\n- UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - **Landscaping & Trees**\n- Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n\nSo Austin Energy HAS reviewed the plans and identified tree clearance requirements as a preliminary design requirement. However, I don't have access to the Bluebeam comments to see what specific issues Austin Energy identified.\n\nThe fact that UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 is referenced as a preliminary design requirement means the plans MUST be revised to address any deficiencies in tree clearances from overhead lines.\n\nNow let me compile all my findings. Based on my research:\n\n## Summary of Findings:\n\n**Applicability**: YES - The site has:\n1. Overhead electric (OHE) distribution lines along the southern property line (Valley View Road)\n2. Overhead electric utility pole(s) at the southeast corner with guy wires\n3. Proposed trees including shade trees (Live Oak, Cedar Elm) and ornamental trees (Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud)\n4. Proposed mitigation trees (species undefined)\n5. Underground electric infrastructure (pull boxes, transformer pads, underground lines)\n\n**Deficiencies Found**:\n\n1. **EL-2.1**: NOT-VERIFIABLE - Multiple trees are positioned within 15 feet of OHE distribution line, but:\n   - Mitigation trees are not identified by species (only marked 'M')\n   - Cannot verify utility compatibility without species identification and ECM Appendix F reference\n\n2. **EL-2.3**: NOT-VERIFIABLE - Multiple trees within 25 feet of OHE distribution line, but:\n   - Plant schedule lists only MINIMUM INSTALLATION HEIGHTS (16', 8', 10')\n   - Does not provide MATURE HEIGHTS needed to determine if trees are \"large trees\" (≥40 ft)\n   - Cedar Elm and Live Oak likely exceed 40 feet at maturity, though this isn't explicitly documented on the plans\n\n3. **EL-2.6**: FAIL - Trees are proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead electric utility pole at the southeast corner with trees directly adjacent/nearby\n\n4. **EL-2.7**: FAIL - Trees potentially within 10 feet of pad-mounted electric equipment, with tree canopies immediately adjacent to the transformer near Building 1 and access doors not indicated on the electrical plan\n\n5. **EL-2.8**: NOT-VERIFIABLE - Trees potentially within 5 feet of underground equipment including multiple pull boxes and underground lines throughout the site. The landscape plan lacks sufficient detail relative to underground equipment locations, making it impossible to verify distances without overlaying the landscape and electrical plans at a larger scale.\n\n6. **EL-2.9**: NOT-VERIFIABLE - Trees within 20 feet of underground equipment may lack root barriers, as no root barrier details are shown and distances cannot be verified without plan overlays.\n\n7. **EL-2.10**: FAIL - Mitigation trees are marked only with 'M' symbols on the plant schedule without species identification, preventing verification of utility compatibility.\n\n8. **EL-2.11**: FAIL - The plant schedule provides only minimum installation heights rather than mature height specifications, making it impossible to determine which proposed trees qualify as \"large trees\" (≥40 feet per ECM Appendix F), though Cedar Elm and Live Oak likely do.\n\nCedar Elm and Live Oak likely qualify as large trees, but this is not documented. Items EL-2.12 and EL-2.13 are not applicable since tree clearances are not dimensioned on the plans. EL-2.14 passes because trees are shown on the landscape plan in relation to the overhead electric line. However, EL-2.15 cannot be verified—while the Master Comment Report references Austin Energy review with Bluebeam comments, I cannot access those comments to confirm Austin Energy approval for trees in restricted zones, and no written approval letter from Austin Energy is included. EL-2.2 is not applicable as only distribution voltage facilities are present, not transmission lines.\n\nEL-2.4 and EL-2.5 are also not applicable since no transmission lines or easements are identified on the plans.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":658,"cache_read_input_tokens":71952,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":658},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dedcba6e-469f-4ff1-8623-d3aaae962125","uuid":"dbefbff8-1301-4796-bf18-146e429172c3"}
{"level":30,"time":1778524284694,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WCN97REZQEnpBsFSimnm8E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have completed my research. Let me compile my findings. Based on my comprehensive review of the site plans, I've identified several deficiencies related to tree clearances from overhead electric lines. Let me generate the structured findings:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":658,"cache_read_input_tokens":71952,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":658},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dedcba6e-469f-4ff1-8623-d3aaae962125","uuid":"b0868c7c-7487-4440-9513-332f4dbeab95"}
{"level":30,"time":1778524284694,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WCN97REZQEnpBsFSimnm8E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016LrtSZWEqXSvpRjTLfkqo1","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property line along Valley View Road where OHE line is located; trees within 15 feet of overhead conductor"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple trees are positioned within 15 lateral feet of the OHE distribution line along the southern property line (at distances of 0.7, 1.0, 1.5, 6, and 11 feet from conductor). However, the species of proposed mitigation trees ('M' symbols near OHE) are not identified in the plant schedule, preventing verification of utility compatibility against ECM Appendix F. Shade tree and ornamental tree species identifications are provided, but their utility-compatible status is not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the landscape plan identified multiple trees within 15 feet of the OHE line at the southern boundary (0.7 to 11 feet from conductor). The plant schedule identifies Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, and Mexican Redbud by name and symbol, but mitigation trees ('M' symbols) visible on the landscape plan are not linked to any species in the plant schedule.","reasoning":"The regulatory requirement specifies that only utility-compatible trees (per ECM Appendix F UC designation) are permitted within 15 feet of distribution conductors. The plant schedule lacks species identification for mitigation trees, and the ECM Appendix F utility-compatible status of the shade and ornamental trees is not documented on the plans. Without both species identity and documented utility compatibility for all trees in this zone, the requirement cannot be verified as met.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property line along Valley View Road where OHE line is located; large trees (40+ feet mature height) within 25 feet of overhead conductor"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple trees are positioned within 25 lateral feet of the OHE distribution line. However, the plant schedule lists only minimum installation heights (Live Oak and Cedar Elm: 16' minimum; Texas Mountain Laurel: 8' minimum; Mexican Redbud: 10' minimum) rather than mature heights. Per ECM Appendix F, large trees are defined as those with mature height ≥40 feet. Without documented mature heights, cannot verify whether proposed trees meet the prohibition against large trees within 25 feet of distribution conductors.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plant schedule on Sheet 35 provides minimum installation heights in the 'MIN. SPEC.' column (e.g., '16' HT. MINIMUM') but does not provide mature height specifications. Cedar Elm and Live Oak are species commonly reaching 40+ feet at maturity, but the plan does not document these mature heights.","reasoning":"The requirement prohibits trees with mature height ≥40 feet from being planted within 25 feet of distribution conductors per UCM § 1.10.10.4. The distinction between installation height and mature height is critical; minimum container-grown specification (16' at planting) does not address eventual mature size. Without documented mature heights in the plant schedule, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast corner of property at overhead electric utility pole location; trees within 10 feet of pole"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"An overhead electric utility pole with guy wire is shown at the southeast corner of the property. Vision analysis identified trees positioned within 10 lateral feet of this pole, including trees directly adjacent to the corner pole location. All tree types are prohibited within 10 feet of utility poles per UCM § 1.10.10.4, regardless of species or size.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the landscape plan identified a utility pole symbol at the southeast corner with guy wire, and multiple tree symbols (both smooth circles for proposed trees and irregular outlines for existing trees) positioned immediately adjacent to this pole, well within 10 feet based on the 1\"=20' scale.","reasoning":"The requirement is a categorical prohibition: trees (any species, any size) are not permitted within 10 lateral feet of any overhead electric utility pole. The presence of tree symbols adjacent to the pole constitutes a clear violation of this requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Pad-mounted transformer equipment locations, particularly Location 1 west of Building 1 and south of entry drive"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Four pad-mounted transformer pads are shown on the electrical design plan (Sheet 21). At least one location (west of Building 1) has large tree canopy symbols immediately adjacent to the pad. Access doors are not indicated on the electrical equipment symbol. Trees are prohibited within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment per UCM § 1.10.10.4. Cannot verify distances and access door orientation without clearer depiction of pad-mounted equipment boundaries and access door locations on plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 identified four labeled 'Electrical Transformer Pad' locations. At Location 1 (west of Bldg 1), vision notes 'The edge of the closest plotted tree canopy appears to be immediately adjacent to or slightly overlapping the area just north of the transformer pad.' The electrical plan symbol shows a simple rectangle with letter 'E' and does not indicate access door location.","reasoning":"The requirement prohibits trees within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment, and additionally restricts trees between equipment access doors and drivable surfaces. The electrical plan does not clearly show pad-mounted equipment boundaries, access door orientations, or the required clearance zones. While trees appear to be positioned very close to at least one pad, the exact distances and access door locations cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Underground electric equipment locations including pull boxes, transformer pads, and underground electric lines throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple underground electric pull boxes, transformer pads, vaults, and underground electric lines are shown on the electrical design plan (Sheet 21). Vision analysis indicates that some pull boxes and underground lines appear to be located near existing and proposed trees. Trees are prohibited within 5 lateral feet of underground electric equipment per UCM § 1.10.10.4. The electrical plan reference note directs readers to 'Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list,' indicating the plans are not fully overlaid. Without a detailed overlay of proposed tree locations and underground equipment at adequate scale, distances cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 identifies multiple 'Electrical Pull Box' locations throughout the site and underground electric lines routing through the property. The vision analysis noted that some appear to intersect or be near tree canopy outlines on that sheet. However, the electrical plan explicitly references the landscape plan for tree details, indicating incomplete correlation.","reasoning":"The requirement prohibits trees within 5 feet of underground electric equipment. The electrical and landscape plans appear to be separate documents not fully overlaid or cross-coordinated for tree-utility distance verification. The electrical plan's reference to 'Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list' confirms that comprehensive verification requires coordinated analysis, which the submitted plans do not facilitate.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":37}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment are required to have root barriers (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment) per UCM § 1.10.10.4. The landscape details sheet (Sheet 37) shows standard tree planting detail specifications but does not identify which trees require root barriers or specify root barrier locations relative to underground equipment. No root barrier specifications are shown on the landscape plan or electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 37 provides standard tree planting details including pit size, stake specifications, and mulch requirements, but does not address root barrier requirements for trees near underground electrical equipment. The landscape plan does not indicate which trees are within 20 feet of underground equipment or show root barrier details.","reasoning":"The requirement for root barriers is conditional on proximity to underground equipment. The plans do not establish which trees fall within the 20-foot trigger distance for this requirement, nor do they show root barrier specifications where required. This prevents verification of compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed near overhead electric facilities along southern property line; specifically mitigation trees (M symbols) visible on landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The plant schedule on Sheet 35 identifies four proposed tree species: Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, and Mexican Redbud, each with a unique symbol. However, the landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows mitigation trees marked only with 'M' symbols without species identification. The plant schedule does not provide a species assignment for the 'M' mitigation tree symbol, preventing verification of which species are being used for mitigation planting near electric facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the plant schedule found that shade trees and ornamental trees are identified by both symbol and species name in the tables on Sheet 35 (e.g., circle with '+' = Live Oak, circle with dot = Cedar Elm, scalloped circle = Texas Mountain Laurel, etc.). However, the 'M' symbol shown on the landscape plan near the OHE line does not appear in the plant schedule tables; the schedule contains no 'MITIGATION TREE' or 'M' symbol specification with an associated species name.","reasoning":"The requirement is that species of trees proposed near electric facilities must be identified to allow verification of utility compatibility and mature height. The absence of species identification for mitigation trees (marked only as 'M') makes it impossible to verify whether these trees meet utility-compatible or size restrictions applicable to their location.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed trees, particularly shade trees (Live Oak, Cedar Elm) and ornamental trees near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The plant schedule lists minimum installation heights (Live Oak and Cedar Elm: '16' HT. MINIMUM'; Texas Mountain Laurel: '8' HT. MINIMUM'; Mexican Redbud: '10' HT. MINIMUM') in the 'MIN. SPEC.' column. However, the schedule does not provide mature height specifications needed to determine which trees qualify as 'large trees' (≥40 feet per ECM Appendix F). Cedar Elm and Live Oak commonly mature to 40+ feet, making them subject to large tree restrictions within 25 feet of distribution conductors, but this mature height is not documented on plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plant schedule on Sheet 35 shows minimum container specifications in the 'MIN. SPEC.' column (e.g., '100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM') but there is no 'MATURE HEIGHT' column in any of the plant schedule tables reviewed. The vision analysis confirmed that only installation heights are listed, not mature heights.","reasoning":"The requirement to differentiate large trees (40+ feet mature height) from other trees is necessary to verify compliance with clearance restrictions. The 16-foot minimum installation height for Live Oak does not indicate that tree's mature height of 40+ feet. Without documented mature heights in the plant schedule, reviewers cannot determine which proposed trees fall under large tree restrictions, creating ambiguity about compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement applies only when overhead transmission lines (60kV or higher) are present or proposed. The site plan shows only distribution-voltage overhead electric facilities (OHE line along southern boundary, typical of local distribution infrastructure). No transmission lines, transmission easements, or transmission-scale infrastructure have been identified. Transmission facilities are physically larger and would be documented with transmission easement notation or significantly larger conductor structures.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis and document review identified only 'OHE' (Overhead Electric) line marking on plans, consistent with distribution voltage (typically 12.47kV or 34.5kV). Facts.md identified 5-foot electric easements (plat-dedicated), which are standard for distribution. No transmission easement plat notes or transmission-voltage labeling were found.","reasoning":"The applicability gate principle requires first determining whether the triggering condition exists. Transmission lines are characterized by voltage ≥60kV, dedicated easements, larger structures, and plat notation. The absence of these indicators, combined with the presence of distribution-voltage markings and smaller easements, provides strong evidence that transmission facilities are not part of this project.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement applies only when overhead transmission lines (60kV or higher) are present or proposed. As documented in the EL-2.2 evaluation, no transmission lines have been identified on this project. Transmission facilities, if present, would be clearly labeled and include transmission easement documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Same observation as EL-2.2: only distribution-voltage infrastructure is documented on the plans.","reasoning":"The applicability gate requires presence of transmission facilities. No transmission lines have been identified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement applies only when transmission easements are present on the site. The grading plan (Sheet 11) depicts various utility easements including drainage, wastewater, and electric easements, but no transmission easement boundaries are shown. The documented easements (5-foot electric easements per facts.md, 10-foot wastewater, 25-foot drainage from adjacent plats) are consistent with distribution infrastructure, not transmission.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows drainage easements, wastewater easements, electric easements, and greenbelt easement, but no transmission easement. Facts.md documents 5-foot electric easements (plat-dedicated), inconsistent with transmission facility scale.","reasoning":"The applicability gate requires presence of transmission easement. No transmission easement has been identified on the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement applies only when tree clearances are dimensioned on plans. The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees and the OHE line but does not include dimension lines or numerical clearance distances between trees and the conductor. No clearance dimensions are provided anywhere on the submitted plan sheets.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan review shows tree symbols and OHE line depiction, but no dimension lines showing distances between trees and conductor.","reasoning":"The requirement addresses measurement methodology when clearances are dimensioned. Since no clearances are dimensioned on the plans, this requirement is inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement applies only when tree clearances are dimensioned on plans. As noted in EL-2.12, no clearance dimensions are provided on the landscape plan or any other submitted sheet.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Same as EL-2.12: no clearance dimensions are shown on plans.","reasoning":"The requirement addresses dimension source methodology when dimensions are present. Since no clearance dimensions are dimensioned, this requirement is inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric facilities along southern property line; landscape plan coverage"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows the OHE (Overhead Electric) line along the southern property boundary with tree symbols positioned in relation to this line. The OHE line is labeled and depicted as a dashed line with text notation ('- OHE -'). Trees are shown as circular symbols throughout the plan and are visible adjacent to the OHE line marking. The requirement to show trees in relation to overhead electric facilities is satisfied.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 31 confirmed that overhead electric line is marked as '- OHE -' along the southern boundary and tree symbols (both existing and proposed) are depicted in relation to this line, particularly near the southern property line.","reasoning":"The requirement is for trees to be shown on the landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities to allow visual verification of proximity and clearances. The submitted landscape plan meets this requirement—the OHE line and tree symbols are both clearly depicted, allowing for spatial relationship assessment.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed within restricted clearance zones: within 15 feet of distribution conductor, within 10 feet of pole, within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"ca29fbe6-6361-4580-848e-7807ae462499","label":"Master Comment Report - Electric Review"}],"comment":"Multiple trees are positioned within the prohibited clearance zones established by UCM § 1.10.10.4 (within 15 feet of distribution conductor, within 10 feet of utility pole). The Master Comment Report indicates that Austin Energy review comments are available on Bluebeam (link provided to external Bluebeam studio), but these comments are not attached to the submitted plan set. Without access to or inclusion of documented written Austin Energy approval authorizing trees in these restricted zones, compliance cannot be verified. Any variation to standard clearance requirements requires explicit written approval from Austin Energy.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Master Comment Report Electric Review section lists 'UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees' as preliminary design requirement and references Austin Energy comments via Bluebeam external link. No written approval letter from Austin Energy is attached to the submitted plans.","reasoning":"The regulatory requirement states that variations to standard clearance distances require explicit written approval from Austin Energy. The plans document multiple instances where trees appear to violate standard clearances (trees within 15 feet of conductor, within 10 feet of pole, within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment). The submission of comments to an external Bluebeam link does not constitute documented approval included in the plan set. Without an attached approval letter from Austin Energy specifically authorizing these clearance variations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":658,"cache_read_input_tokens":71952,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":658},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dedcba6e-469f-4ff1-8623-d3aaae962125","uuid":"c099f958-ef93-40ee-8f95-4261f9f5f954"}
