{"level":30,"time":1778524284694,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_017NJPxezNQwASBkzntYjcx3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I've successfully completed the site plan review for Grouping 2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines). I've evaluated all 15 checklist items and provided detailed findings with agent traces, code citations, and specific observations.\n\nSummary of my findings:\n- **4 items marked as FAIL**: EL-2.6 (trees within 10 feet of utility pole), EL-2.10 (mitigation trees not identified by species), EL-2.11 (large trees not differentiated with mature heights)\n- **6 items marked as NOT-VERIFIABLE**: EL-2.1, EL-2.3, EL-2.7, EL-2.8, EL-2.9, EL-2.15\n- **4 items marked as N/A**: EL-2.2, EL-2.4, EL-2.5 (transmission-related, not applicable), EL-2.12, EL-2.13 (no dimensions shown)\n- **1 item marked as PASS**: EL-2.14 (trees are shown on landscape plan)\n\nAll findings include detailed observations, reasoning, and citations to the applicable code sections.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6985,"cache_read_input_tokens":72610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6985},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dedcba6e-469f-4ff1-8623-d3aaae962125","uuid":"df2cdebb-5d0e-4cf8-b89c-c9ba7cb60a4f"}
{"level":30,"time":1778524284694,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_017NJPxezNQwASBkzntYjcx3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the comprehensive site plan review for Grouping 2: **Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines**.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nI evaluated all 15 checklist items and found the following:\n\n### **Critical Deficiencies Identified (4 FAIL):**\n\n1. **EL-2.6 - Trees within 10 feet of utility pole**: FAIL\n   - Overhead electric pole with guy wire at southeast corner has trees positioned directly adjacent to it\n   - Clear violation of categorical prohibition\n\n2. **EL-2.10 - Plant species not identified**: FAIL  \n   - Mitigation trees ('M' symbols on landscape plan) are not identified by species\n   - Plant schedule lists shade and ornamental tree species but not mitigation tree species\n   - Prevents verification of utility compatibility\n\n3. **EL-2.11 - Large trees not differentiated**: FAIL\n   - Plant schedule provides only minimum installation heights (16', 8', 10')\n   - Does not provide mature heights needed to identify large trees (≥40 feet per ECM Appendix F)\n   - Cedar Elm and Live Oak likely mature to 40+ feet but this is undocumented\n\n### **Items Requiring Clarification (6 NOT-VERIFIABLE):**\n\n1. **EL-2.1** - Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 feet of distribution conductor\n2. **EL-2.3** - Large trees within 25 feet of distribution conductor  \n3. **EL-2.7** - Trees within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment\n4. **EL-2.8** - Trees within 5 feet of underground equipment\n5. **EL-2.9** - Root barriers not shown for trees within 20 feet of underground equipment\n6. **EL-2.15** - No documented Austin Energy approval for trees in restricted zones\n\n### **Not Applicable Items (4):**\n\n- **EL-2.2, EL-2.4, EL-2.5** - Transmission-related requirements (only distribution lines present)\n- **EL-2.12, EL-2.13** - Measurement methodology (no clearances dimensioned on plans)\n\n### **Compliant Item (1 PASS):**\n\n- **EL-2.14** - Trees ARE shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities ✓\n\nAll findings have been documented with detailed observations, regulatory citations, and visual evidence references. The review identifies critical gaps in the plant schedule (missing species for mitigation trees, missing mature heights) and potential clearance violations near overhead poles and equipment that require applicant response."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6985,"cache_read_input_tokens":72610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6985},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dedcba6e-469f-4ff1-8623-d3aaae962125","uuid":"c95b14fd-1886-4b14-9217-2b8793bbb172"}
{"level":30,"time":1778524284695,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":4088734,"duration_api_ms":206125,"num_turns":29,"result":"I have completed the comprehensive site plan review for Grouping 2: **Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines**.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nI evaluated all 15 checklist items and found the following:\n\n### **Critical Deficiencies Identified (4 FAIL):**\n\n1. **EL-2.6 - Trees within 10 feet of utility pole**: FAIL\n   - Overhead electric pole with guy wire at southeast corner has trees positioned directly adjacent to it\n   - Clear violation of categorical prohibition\n\n2. **EL-2.10 - Plant species not identified**: FAIL  \n   - Mitigation trees ('M' symbols on landscape plan) are not identified by species\n   - Plant schedule lists shade and ornamental tree species but not mitigation tree species\n   - Prevents verification of utility compatibility\n\n3. **EL-2.11 - Large trees not differentiated**: FAIL\n   - Plant schedule provides only minimum installation heights (16', 8', 10')\n   - Does not provide mature heights needed to identify large trees (≥40 feet per ECM Appendix F)\n   - Cedar Elm and Live Oak likely mature to 40+ feet but this is undocumented\n\n### **Items Requiring Clarification (6 NOT-VERIFIABLE):**\n\n1. **EL-2.1** - Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 feet of distribution conductor\n2. **EL-2.3** - Large trees within 25 feet of distribution conductor  \n3. **EL-2.7** - Trees within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment\n4. **EL-2.8** - Trees within 5 feet of underground equipment\n5. **EL-2.9** - Root barriers not shown for trees within 20 feet of underground equipment\n6. **EL-2.15** - No documented Austin Energy approval for trees in restricted zones\n\n### **Not Applicable Items (4):**\n\n- **EL-2.2, EL-2.4, EL-2.5** - Transmission-related requirements (only distribution lines present)\n- **EL-2.12, EL-2.13** - Measurement methodology (no clearances dimensioned on plans)\n\n### **Compliant Item (1 PASS):**\n\n- **EL-2.14** - Trees ARE shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities ✓\n\nAll findings have been documented with detailed observations, regulatory citations, and visual evidence references. The review identifies critical gaps in the plant schedule (missing species for mitigation trees, missing mature heights) and potential clearance violations near overhead poles and equipment that require applicant response.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"dedcba6e-469f-4ff1-8623-d3aaae962125","total_cost_usd":0.3073428,"usage":{"input_tokens":172,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60636,"cache_read_input_tokens":1324958,"output_tokens":19776,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":60636,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":172,"outputTokens":19776,"cacheReadInputTokens":1324958,"cacheCreationInputTokens":60636,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3073428,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property line along Valley View Road where OHE line is located; trees within 15 feet of overhead conductor"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple trees are positioned within 15 lateral feet of the OHE distribution line along the southern property line (at distances of 0.7, 1.0, 1.5, 6, and 11 feet from conductor). However, the species of proposed mitigation trees ('M' symbols near OHE) are not identified in the plant schedule, preventing verification of utility compatibility against ECM Appendix F. Shade tree and ornamental tree species identifications are provided, but their utility-compatible status is not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the landscape plan identified multiple trees within 15 feet of the OHE line at the southern boundary (0.7 to 11 feet from conductor). The plant schedule identifies Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, and Mexican Redbud by name and symbol, but mitigation trees ('M' symbols) visible on the landscape plan are not linked to any species in the plant schedule.","reasoning":"The regulatory requirement specifies that only utility-compatible trees (per ECM Appendix F UC designation) are permitted within 15 feet of distribution conductors. The plant schedule lacks species identification for mitigation trees, and the ECM Appendix F utility-compatible status of the shade and ornamental trees is not documented on the plans. Without both species identity and documented utility compatibility for all trees in this zone, the requirement cannot be verified as met.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property line along Valley View Road where OHE line is located; large trees (40+ feet mature height) within 25 feet of overhead conductor"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple trees are positioned within 25 lateral feet of the OHE distribution line. However, the plant schedule lists only minimum installation heights (Live Oak and Cedar Elm: 16' minimum; Texas Mountain Laurel: 8' minimum; Mexican Redbud: 10' minimum) rather than mature heights. Per ECM Appendix F, large trees are defined as those with mature height ≥40 feet. Without documented mature heights, cannot verify whether proposed trees meet the prohibition against large trees within 25 feet of distribution conductors.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plant schedule on Sheet 35 provides minimum installation heights in the 'MIN. SPEC.' column (e.g., '16' HT. MINIMUM') but does not provide mature height specifications. Cedar Elm and Live Oak are species commonly reaching 40+ feet at maturity, but the plan does not document these mature heights.","reasoning":"The requirement prohibits trees with mature height ≥40 feet from being planted within 25 feet of distribution conductors per UCM § 1.10.10.4. The distinction between installation height and mature height is critical; minimum container-grown specification (16' at planting) does not address eventual mature size. Without documented mature heights in the plant schedule, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast corner of property at overhead electric utility pole location; trees within 10 feet of pole"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"An overhead electric utility pole with guy wire is shown at the southeast corner of the property. Vision analysis identified trees positioned within 10 lateral feet of this pole, including trees directly adjacent to the corner pole location. All tree types are prohibited within 10 feet of utility poles per UCM § 1.10.10.4, regardless of species or size.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the landscape plan identified a utility pole symbol at the southeast corner with guy wire, and multiple tree symbols (both smooth circles for proposed trees and irregular outlines for existing trees) positioned immediately adjacent to this pole, well within 10 feet based on the 1\"=20' scale.","reasoning":"The requirement is a categorical prohibition: trees (any species, any size) are not permitted within 10 lateral feet of any overhead electric utility pole. The presence of tree symbols adjacent to the pole constitutes a clear violation of this requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Pad-mounted transformer equipment locations, particularly Location 1 west of Building 1 and south of entry drive"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Four pad-mounted transformer pads are shown on the electrical design plan (Sheet 21). At least one location (west of Building 1) has large tree canopy symbols immediately adjacent to the pad. Access doors are not indicated on the electrical equipment symbol. Trees are prohibited within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment per UCM § 1.10.10.4. Cannot verify distances and access door orientation without clearer depiction of pad-mounted equipment boundaries and access door locations on plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 identified four labeled 'Electrical Transformer Pad' locations. At Location 1 (west of Bldg 1), vision notes 'The edge of the closest plotted tree canopy appears to be immediately adjacent to or slightly overlapping the area just north of the transformer pad.' The electrical plan symbol shows a simple rectangle with letter 'E' and does not indicate access door location.","reasoning":"The requirement prohibits trees within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment, and additionally restricts trees between equipment access doors and drivable surfaces. The electrical plan does not clearly show pad-mounted equipment boundaries, access door orientations, or the required clearance zones. While trees appear to be positioned very close to at least one pad, the exact distances and access door locations cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Underground electric equipment locations including pull boxes, transformer pads, and underground electric lines throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple underground electric pull boxes, transformer pads, vaults, and underground electric lines are shown on the electrical design plan (Sheet 21). Vision analysis indicates that some pull boxes and underground lines appear to be located near existing and proposed trees. Trees are prohibited within 5 lateral feet of underground electric equipment per UCM § 1.10.10.4. The electrical plan reference note directs readers to 'Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list,' indicating the plans are not fully overlaid. Without a detailed overlay of proposed tree locations and underground equipment at adequate scale, distances cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 identifies multiple 'Electrical Pull Box' locations throughout the site and underground electric lines routing through the property. The vision analysis noted that some appear to intersect or be near tree canopy outlines on that sheet. However, the electrical plan explicitly references the landscape plan for tree details, indicating incomplete correlation.","reasoning":"The requirement prohibits trees within 5 feet of underground electric equipment. The electrical and landscape plans appear to be separate documents not fully overlaid or cross-coordinated for tree-utility distance verification. The electrical plan's reference to 'Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list' confirms that comprehensive verification requires coordinated analysis, which the submitted plans do not facilitate.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":37}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment are required to have root barriers (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment) per UCM § 1.10.10.4. The landscape details sheet (Sheet 37) shows standard tree planting detail specifications but does not identify which trees require root barriers or specify root barrier locations relative to underground equipment. No root barrier specifications are shown on the landscape plan or electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 37 provides standard tree planting details including pit size, stake specifications, and mulch requirements, but does not address root barrier requirements for trees near underground electrical equipment. The landscape plan does not indicate which trees are within 20 feet of underground equipment or show root barrier details.","reasoning":"The requirement for root barriers is conditional on proximity to underground equipment. The plans do not establish which trees fall within the 20-foot trigger distance for this requirement, nor do they show root barrier specifications where required. This prevents verification of compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed near overhead electric facilities along southern property line; specifically mitigation trees (M symbols) visible on landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The plant schedule on Sheet 35 identifies four proposed tree species: Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, and Mexican Redbud, each with a unique symbol. However, the landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows mitigation trees marked only with 'M' symbols without species identification. The plant schedule does not provide a species assignment for the 'M' mitigation tree symbol, preventing verification of which species are being used for mitigation planting near electric facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the plant schedule found that shade trees and ornamental trees are identified by both symbol and species name in the tables on Sheet 35 (e.g., circle with '+' = Live Oak, circle with dot = Cedar Elm, scalloped circle = Texas Mountain Laurel, etc.). However, the 'M' symbol shown on the landscape plan near the OHE line does not appear in the plant schedule tables; the schedule contains no 'MITIGATION TREE' or 'M' symbol specification with an associated species name.","reasoning":"The requirement is that species of trees proposed near electric facilities must be identified to allow verification of utility compatibility and mature height. The absence of species identification for mitigation trees (marked only as 'M') makes it impossible to verify whether these trees meet utility-compatible or size restrictions applicable to their location.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed trees, particularly shade trees (Live Oak, Cedar Elm) and ornamental trees near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The plant schedule lists minimum installation heights (Live Oak and Cedar Elm: '16' HT. MINIMUM'; Texas Mountain Laurel: '8' HT. MINIMUM'; Mexican Redbud: '10' HT. MINIMUM') in the 'MIN. SPEC.' column. However, the schedule does not provide mature height specifications needed to determine which trees qualify as 'large trees' (≥40 feet per ECM Appendix F). Cedar Elm and Live Oak commonly mature to 40+ feet, making them subject to large tree restrictions within 25 feet of distribution conductors, but this mature height is not documented on plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plant schedule on Sheet 35 shows minimum container specifications in the 'MIN. SPEC.' column (e.g., '100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM') but there is no 'MATURE HEIGHT' column in any of the plant schedule tables reviewed. The vision analysis confirmed that only installation heights are listed, not mature heights.","reasoning":"The requirement to differentiate large trees (40+ feet mature height) from other trees is necessary to verify compliance with clearance restrictions. The 16-foot minimum installation height for Live Oak does not indicate that tree's mature height of 40+ feet. Without documented mature heights in the plant schedule, reviewers cannot determine which proposed trees fall under large tree restrictions, creating ambiguity about compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement applies only when overhead transmission lines (60kV or higher) are present or proposed. The site plan shows only distribution-voltage overhead electric facilities (OHE line along southern boundary, typical of local distribution infrastructure). No transmission lines, transmission easements, or transmission-scale infrastructure have been identified. Transmission facilities are physically larger and would be documented with transmission easement notation or significantly larger conductor structures.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis and document review identified only 'OHE' (Overhead Electric) line marking on plans, consistent with distribution voltage (typically 12.47kV or 34.5kV). Facts.md identified 5-foot electric easements (plat-dedicated), which are standard for distribution. No transmission easement plat notes or transmission-voltage labeling were found.","reasoning":"The applicability gate principle requires first determining whether the triggering condition exists. Transmission lines are characterized by voltage ≥60kV, dedicated easements, larger structures, and plat notation. The absence of these indicators, combined with the presence of distribution-voltage markings and smaller easements, provides strong evidence that transmission facilities are not part of this project.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement applies only when overhead transmission lines (60kV or higher) are present or proposed. As documented in the EL-2.2 evaluation, no transmission lines have been identified on this project. Transmission facilities, if present, would be clearly labeled and include transmission easement documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Same observation as EL-2.2: only distribution-voltage infrastructure is documented on the plans.","reasoning":"The applicability gate requires presence of transmission facilities. No transmission lines have been identified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement applies only when transmission easements are present on the site. The grading plan (Sheet 11) depicts various utility easements including drainage, wastewater, and electric easements, but no transmission easement boundaries are shown. The documented easements (5-foot electric easements per facts.md, 10-foot wastewater, 25-foot drainage from adjacent plats) are consistent with distribution infrastructure, not transmission.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows drainage easements, wastewater easements, electric easements, and greenbelt easement, but no transmission easement. Facts.md documents 5-foot electric easements (plat-dedicated), inconsistent with transmission facility scale.","reasoning":"The applicability gate requires presence of transmission easement. No transmission easement has been identified on the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement applies only when tree clearances are dimensioned on plans. The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees and the OHE line but does not include dimension lines or numerical clearance distances between trees and the conductor. No clearance dimensions are provided anywhere on the submitted plan sheets.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan review shows tree symbols and OHE line depiction, but no dimension lines showing distances between trees and conductor.","reasoning":"The requirement addresses measurement methodology when clearances are dimensioned. Since no clearances are dimensioned on the plans, this requirement is inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement applies only when tree clearances are dimensioned on plans. As noted in EL-2.12, no clearance dimensions are provided on the landscape plan or any other submitted sheet.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Same as EL-2.12: no clearance dimensions are shown on plans.","reasoning":"The requirement addresses dimension source methodology when dimensions are present. Since no clearance dimensions are dimensioned, this requirement is inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric facilities along southern property line; landscape plan coverage"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows the OHE (Overhead Electric) line along the southern property boundary with tree symbols positioned in relation to this line. The OHE line is labeled and depicted as a dashed line with text notation ('- OHE -'). Trees are shown as circular symbols throughout the plan and are visible adjacent to the OHE line marking. The requirement to show trees in relation to overhead electric facilities is satisfied.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 31 confirmed that overhead electric line is marked as '- OHE -' along the southern boundary and tree symbols (both existing and proposed) are depicted in relation to this line, particularly near the southern property line.","reasoning":"The requirement is for trees to be shown on the landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities to allow visual verification of proximity and clearances. The submitted landscape plan meets this requirement—the OHE line and tree symbols are both clearly depicted, allowing for spatial relationship assessment.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed within restricted clearance zones: within 15 feet of distribution conductor, within 10 feet of pole, within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"ca29fbe6-6361-4580-848e-7807ae462499","label":"Master Comment Report - Electric Review"}],"comment":"Multiple trees are positioned within the prohibited clearance zones established by UCM § 1.10.10.4 (within 15 feet of distribution conductor, within 10 feet of utility pole). The Master Comment Report indicates that Austin Energy review comments are available on Bluebeam (link provided to external Bluebeam studio), but these comments are not attached to the submitted plan set. Without access to or inclusion of documented written Austin Energy approval authorizing trees in these restricted zones, compliance cannot be verified. Any variation to standard clearance requirements requires explicit written approval from Austin Energy.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Master Comment Report Electric Review section lists 'UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees' as preliminary design requirement and references Austin Energy comments via Bluebeam external link. No written approval letter from Austin Energy is attached to the submitted plans.","reasoning":"The regulatory requirement states that variations to standard clearance distances require explicit written approval from Austin Energy. The plans document multiple instances where trees appear to violate standard clearances (trees within 15 feet of conductor, within 10 feet of pole, within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment). The submission of comments to an external Bluebeam link does not constitute documented approval included in the plan set. Without an attached approval letter from Austin Energy specifically authorizing these clearance variations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0260d5f5-f1f2-411c-b49c-06e56d404b58"}
{"level":30,"time":1778524284695,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_016MmJSdHR3gArqNSrt1jszq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ay6n8m68YddQkMYbmi95vW","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads west of Buildings 2 and 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Measured clearances from transformer pads to adjacent buildings: west of Bldg 2 = 12.8 feet, west of Bldg 8 = 8 feet. Both exceed the 5-foot minimum requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of two transformer pads on Sheet 9 shows distances of 12.8 feet and 8 feet from the nearest building exterior walls.","reasoning":"Both measured distances exceed the 5-foot minimum clearance threshold specified in the code. The requirement is satisfied for the measured transformer pads.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No retaining walls are adjacent to transformer pads. The requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Examination of site plan (Sheet 9) and grading plan (Sheet 11) shows retaining walls located around site perimeter and pond, but none adjacent to transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"The item is conditionally applicable only when retaining walls are present adjacent to transformer pads. No such proximity exists on this project.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fences or gates are adjacent to transformer pads. The requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review shows no fence lines or gates in proximity to any transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"This requirement is conditionally applicable only when fences/gates are adjacent to transformer pads. No such condition exists on this project.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are labeled on the site plan or electrical plan. Cannot verify whether clearances less than 5 feet are present or whether required AE Design written approval and fire rating documentation are provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of Sheets 9 and 21 confirms no numerical dimension callouts specifying clearances from transformer pads to buildings are provided.","reasoning":"Without specific dimension callouts, it cannot be determined whether any transformer pads have reduced clearances requiring AE Design approval. The requirement cannot be evaluated.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No balconies or overhangs are shown above or adjacent to transformer pads. No covering or structure is directly above transformer pads. The requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and grading plan review shows no building overhangs, balconies, or structures positioned above transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"This requirement is conditionally applicable only when balconies or overhangs are present. No such condition exists.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on the plans. No dimension callouts show clearance distances from windows, doors, or ventilating ducts. Requirement applicability and compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan notes and site plan do not specify whether transformers are oil-filled or dry-type, and no dimensions are provided for clearances to building windows, doors, or ducts.","reasoning":"This requirement applies specifically to oil-filled equipment and requires verification of specific distance measurements. Without this information, compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No sidewalks are shown on the electrical plan near transformer pads. No dimension callouts specify distance from sidewalk edges. Cannot verify compliance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plans do not provide dimension callouts showing distances from transformer pad edges to any sidewalk edges.","reasoning":"While sidewalks exist on the site, the specific proximity relationship between sidewalk edges and transformer pads cannot be verified from the available dimensions.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairwells serving as fire exits are adjacent to transformer pad locations. The requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building floor plans and fire protection plan show no stairwells positioned adjacent to transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"This requirement is conditionally applicable only when stairwells are present adjacent to transformers. No such condition exists on this project.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not shown on the fire protection plan. No fire escape or stair locations are identified relative to transformer pads. Equipment type (oil-filled) is not specified. Cannot verify 20-foot clearance requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire protection plan (Sheet 10) does not depict transformer pads, and no fire escape locations are shown on sheets containing transformer pads.","reasoning":"Fire escape clearances apply specifically to oil-filled equipment, which is not identified on these plans. The requirement cannot be evaluated without knowing equipment type and fire escape proximity.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad access door sides are not oriented or labeled on any plan sheet. Clearance distances to open area or buildings are not dimensioned for most pads. Only one measurement of 54.1 feet was obtained; insufficient data to verify all pads meet 10-foot minimum.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of electrical and site plans shows transformer pads with no access door orientation indicators or dimensions from pad edges to buildings/open areas.","reasoning":"Without access door orientation and specific distance callouts for each pad, compliance with the 10-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified for all transformer locations.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer locations are within niches, vaults, or enclosed areas on 3+ sides. The requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review shows all transformer pads located in open areas of the property, not within building footprints or niche configurations.","reasoning":"This requirement is conditionally applicable only when transformers are located in confined spaces. No niche configurations are proposed on this project.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"One fire hydrant is shown on the fire protection plan, but no dimension callouts specify its distance from transformer pad locations. Cannot verify 5-foot clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire protection plan shows one private fire hydrant location, but no dimensions relate this to transformer pad positions.","reasoning":"The specific distance between the fire hydrant and transformer pads cannot be determined from the plans provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are not shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31). Tree locations cannot be cross-referenced to transformer pads to verify utility-compatible species within 10-15 lateral feet. Landscape notes reference Sheet 32 tree list but tree coordinates relative to transformer pads are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows vegetation and tree locations, but transformer pad symbols are not depicted on this sheet.","reasoning":"Without transformer pad locations shown on the landscape plan, proximity relationships between trees and transformers cannot be evaluated.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are not shown on the landscape plan. Shrub and groundcover planting locations cannot be cross-referenced to transformer pads to verify 10-foot and 5-foot clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transformer pads are not depicted on the landscape plan (Sheet 31), preventing verification of vegetation clearances.","reasoning":"Cross-referencing between vegetation locations and transformer access door orientation requires transformer symbols on the landscape plan, which are absent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":37}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are not shown on the landscape plan or detail sheets. Trees within 20 lateral feet cannot be identified, and root barrier details specific to transformer equipment cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of landscape plan and detail sheets shows no transformer pad symbols.","reasoning":"Without transformer locations identified on the landscape plan, the 20-foot tree proximity trigger and required root barrier specifications cannot be evaluated.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dumpsters or trash enclosures are adjacent to transformer pad locations. The requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review shows trash collection areas, but no dumpster or trash enclosure is positioned adjacent to transformer pads.","reasoning":"This requirement is conditionally applicable only when dumpsters are present adjacent to transformers. No such condition exists.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No bike racks are adjacent to transformer pad locations. The requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Bicycle parking is shown on the site plan within building garages, but no bike racks are positioned adjacent to transformer pads.","reasoning":"This requirement is conditionally applicable only when bike racks are adjacent to transformers. No such condition exists.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No light poles are adjacent to transformer pad locations. The requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":