"tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are not shown on the utility plan (Sheet 19) alongside underground utility routes. No dimension callouts specify 12-inch horizontal and vertical separation from water, wastewater, or electric conduits. Cannot verify minimum clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan shows underground utilities but transformer pads are not depicted on this sheet, preventing cross-reference of separations.","reasoning":"The 12-inch clearance requirement requires transformer locations to be shown on the same utility plan as other buried infrastructure. This comparison is not possible from available plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are shown on separate plan sheets (Site Plan, Electrical Plan) but are not overlaid with utility line routing on a single sheet showing the relationship between transformer pads and underground/overhead utility locations. Cannot verify that transformers or AE facilities are not located over/under other utility lines or building structures.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transformer pads are depicted on Sheets 9 and 21, while utilities are shown on Sheet 19. These sheets are not overlaid to verify conflicts.","reasoning":"Verification of cross-utility conflicts and placement over/under other infrastructure requires overlay of transformer locations with utility and building structure locations, which is not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution lines are shown on or near the property. Utilities are served by underground lines. The requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and utility plan review shows underground utility service with no overhead distribution conductors shown on or adjacent to the property.","reasoning":"This requirement is conditionally applicable only when overhead distribution lines are present. Underground service is provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors are shown on the property. Underground electric service is provided. The requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility documentation indicates underground electric service throughout the site.","reasoning":"This requirement is conditionally applicable only when overhead distribution conductors are present. The project has underground electrical service.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer locations are within niches or enclosed areas. All transformer pads are located in open site areas. Niche service is not proposed. The requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and grading plan show all transformer pads located in open site areas, not within building footprints.","reasoning":"This requirement is conditionally applicable only when transformers are installed in niche configurations. Standard pad-mounted service is proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Niche service installations are not proposed. All transformers are pad-mounted in open site areas. The requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan configuration shows transformer pads located outside building footprints in open areas.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to niche service installations where AE equipment is within a building footprint. This configuration is not proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas are positioned above transformer pads. No vertical clearance cross-sections are required. The requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review shows transformer pads in open areas with no structures above them.","reasoning":"This requirement is conditionally applicable only when overhead structures exist above transformers. No such configuration is proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on the plans. Grading plan does not show surface flow direction specifically relative to transformer pad locations or indicate whether liquid/drainage flows away from buildings. Cannot verify drainage direction requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan does not specify equipment type, and grading plan does not identify surface flow direction specifically at transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment and requires verification that surface grading directs liquid flow away from buildings. Without equipment type specification and specific grading callouts at pads, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are not explicitly annotated as being 100% on private property. Subdivision plat (Sheet 2) shows property lines and easements, but transformer locations are not cross-referenced to confirm they are entirely within private property boundaries and not straddling property lines or located in public right-of-way.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transformer pads are shown on site plan but no annotations explicitly state they are located on private property. Plat sheet shows easements and property boundaries.","reasoning":"Verification requires explicit confirmation that each transformer pad's entire footprint is on private property and not in ROW. This confirmation is not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Facts.md indicates multiple recorded easements including drainage easements, wastewater easements, electric easements, and water easements. Site plan depicts easements but transformer pad locations are not explicitly annotated as being outside prohibited easement areas or noting AE Design written approvals for any easement encroachments.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Project facts document confirms existence of multiple easements (drainage, wastewater, water, electric). Site plan shows these easements, but transformer locations are not explicitly cross-referenced to confirm they avoid prohibited easement areas.","reasoning":"Compliance requires explicit verification that transformer pads are not located in drainage, water, sewer, or overhead electric easements except with AE Design written approval. This verification is not documented.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad easements are not explicitly shown or labeled on any plan sheet. No easement width specifications or AE Design accessibility requirements are documented. Cannot verify that required transformer easements are shown or adequately sized.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and electrical plan show transformer pads but do not depict or label transformer easement boundaries or dimensions.","reasoning":"Verification requires explicit easement delineation with AE Design-required dimensions. This documentation is not provided on the plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical plan shows electric service routing from transformers to meters, but no annotation explicitly confirms that the entire electrical routing is 100% on private property. The extent of electrical routing paths and property line relationships are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows electric lines connecting transformers to meters but does not provide annotations confirming private property location of these routing paths.","reasoning":"Compliance requires explicit documentation that all electrical service lines from transformer to meter are entirely on private property. This verification is not documented.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions (width and length) are not specified on the site plan or electrical plan. Service type (single-phase or three-phase) is not identified. No references to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are provided. Pad dimensions must be confirmed against AE Design specifications for the service type and load.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of Sheets 9 and 21 confirms that transformer pads are shown with no dimensional callouts (e.g., '5x5', '8x8') and no references to AE Design detail sheets or service type specifications.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates that pad dimensions match AE Design-approved details for the specified service type. Without any dimensions labeled and no AE Design detail references, this requirement cannot be met.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad west of Building 2 / near parking area"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"One transformer pad is located within 4 feet of the vehicle circulation route and parking area (abutting the main driveway). No bollard protection is shown around this transformer pad. Bollards are shown elsewhere on the site plan (near units 301, 405, 705), confirming the drafter's knowledge of bollard notation. Required 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal posts must be added to protect the transformer pad within the 4-foot parking/vehicle circulation zone.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of the transformer pad west of Building 2 shows it positioned immediately adjacent to (within 4 feet of) the primary vehicle circulation aisle. Vision review confirms no bollard symbols are drawn at this transformer pad location, though bollard symbols are visible elsewhere on the site plan.","reasoning":"The transformer pad is within the 4-foot triggering distance from parking/vehicle routes, requiring bollard protection per AE Design details. The absence of bollards at this pad while they are shown at other locations on the site constitutes a deficiency.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution facilities are present on the property. Underground electric service is provided. No customer structures are proposed to be installed under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution lines. The requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility and site plans confirm underground electric service with no overhead distribution lines shown.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when overhead distribution facilities are present. The project has underground electrical service.","tools_used":[]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"30f09277-47ef-4956-9ccd-c0950405b0e7"}
{"level":30,"time":1778524284696,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QXwAiXEF4Wnbr6DaPBVmH3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SCdvwYawwWdLSBmUh5ztWt","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad west of Building 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad located west of Building 8 (Unit 801) has only 4.9 feet horizontal clearance from the building wall. Minimum required clearance is 5 feet. Applicant must reposition transformer pad or obtain written Austin Energy Design approval for reduced clearance and provide documentation of 3-hour fire rating and other required conditions per footnote 2.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement on Sheet 9 (Site Plan) measured the distance from the transformer pad west of Building 8 to the west exterior wall of Unit 801 and found 4.9 feet.","reasoning":"The UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 requires minimum 5-foot clearance from buildings and structures. 4.9 feet is below the 5-foot minimum, constituting a deficiency. No AE Design written approval for reduced clearance was provided on the plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No retaining walls are adjacent to transformer pad locations on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheet 9 (Site Plan) confirmed no retaining walls are located adjacent to or near any of the five transformer pads shown.","reasoning":"The requirement only applies when retaining walls are present adjacent to transformer pads. Since no retaining walls are adjacent to transformer pads, this item is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fences or gates are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan and electrical plan found no fence or gate callouts immediately adjacent to any transformer pad.","reasoning":"This requirement only applies when fences or gates are adjacent to transformer pads. Site plan shows no such features adjacent to transformer pads.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer pads show clearances less than 5 feet to brick/masonry buildings with a request for reduced clearance exception. EL-13.1 violation (4.9 feet) is a clearance deficiency, not a reduced clearance exception.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The single clearance violation found (4.9 feet) does not represent a documented request for reduced clearance with supporting documentation; it is simply a failure to meet the standard 5-foot minimum.","reasoning":"This item addresses situations where plans explicitly show reduced clearance (e.g., 3 feet) with supporting approvals and documentation. The deficiency found is a standard clearance failure, not a reduced clearance exception scenario.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No balconies, overhangs, or structures are shown directly above or adjacent to any transformer pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan and building elevations found no balconies or overhangs positioned above or adjacent to any transformer pad.","reasoning":"This requirement only applies when balconies or overhangs are present above or adjacent to transformer pads. The site plan shows no such features.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building windows, doors, or ventilating ducts are shown with inadequate lateral separation or low-grade elevation adjacent to transformer pads. This requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment and only when windows/doors/ducts are present with inadequate separation or low elevation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and building elevation review found no windows, doors, or ventilating ducts positioned adjacent to transformer pads with separations less than 5 feet laterally or less than 12 feet horizontally.","reasoning":"The 12-foot clearance requirement applies only when oil-filled equipment is present (equipment type not specified on plans) AND windows/doors/ducts are present with inadequate lateral separation. No such configurations were identified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad west of Building 2"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad west of Building 2 is located 10.2 feet from the back of the adjacent sidewalk, which exceeds the 2-foot minimum requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement on Sheet 9 measured 10.2 feet from the back edge of the sidewalk adjacent to the transformer pad west of Building 2.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies minimum 2 feet clearance from back of sidewalks. 10.2 feet exceeds this minimum, so the requirement is satisfied.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairwells serving as fire exits are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan found no fire exit stairwells positioned adjacent to any transformer pad.","reasoning":"This requirement only applies when stairwells serving as fire exits are present adjacent to transformer pads. No such features are shown on the plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on electrical plan or any supplementary documents. The 20-foot fire escape clearance requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment. Equipment type must be confirmed from Austin Energy Design transformer specifications to determine applicability of this requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) and all supplementary documents do not specify whether transformers are oil-filled or dry-type. No ESPA or AE Design equipment specifications were provided.","reasoning":"This requirement is gated by equipment type - it only applies to oil-filled equipment. Without confirmation of equipment type from AE Design specifications, applicability cannot be determined.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad located between Buildings 7 and 6 (east of Building 7)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad hot-stick use area (access door side) has only 0.6 feet clearance to adjacent building, when minimum 10-foot clearance to open area or adjacent building/structure is required. This transformer pad is essentially adjacent to (touching) the building wall with virtually no clearance. Applicant must reposition transformer pad to achieve minimum 10-foot hot-stick use area clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement on Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) measured the distance from the access door side of the transformer pad (east of Building 7, between Buildings 7 and 6) to the nearest building exterior wall and found only 0.6 feet.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 requires minimum 10-foot hot-stick use area clearance from the access door side to open area or adjacent building/structure. 0.6 feet is a critical violation, indicating the transformer pad is essentially adjacent to the building with no usable clearance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings or site configuration details provided to determine if any transformer pad location faces a confined space (niche, vault, or enclosed area on 3+ sides) requiring 15-foot hot-stick clearance instead of 10-foot standard clearance. This cannot be verified from plan view alone.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Reviewed all available sheets and found no cross-section drawings showing vertical/depth relationships between transformer pads and potential enclosed areas. Site plan shows plan view only.","reasoning":"Determining if a location 'faces' a confined space requires understanding the 3-dimensional spatial relationship between the access door side and surrounding features. This requires cross-section drawings which are not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire hydrants are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on the site plan. The only private fire hydrant shown on the site plan is located remotely from all transformer pads.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan found one private fire hydrant location remote from transformer pads, with no hydrants adjacent to any transformer pad.","reasoning":"This requirement only applies when fire hydrants are present adjacent to transformer pads. No such proximity conditions exist on the site plan.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The nearest tree to any transformer pad is located 21.5 feet away, exceeding the 10-foot proximity threshold. All proposed trees are species that are utility-compatible or otherwise appropriate for proximity to electrical infrastructure (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel). Vegetation clearance requirements are met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement on Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) identified a tree labeled 'M' (mitigation tree) 21.5 feet from nearest transformer pad. Landscape plan list (Sheet 35) specifies Cedar Elm and Live Oak as shade trees, with both being ECM Appendix F utility-compatible species.","reasoning":"The 10-foot proximity threshold that would trigger utility-compatible species requirements is not met - the nearest tree is 21.5 feet away. Therefore, this requirement is satisfied even without detailed species verification.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas near transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows shrub and groundcover plantings on site, but specific shrub and groundcover plant locations relative to transformer pad access doors cannot be precisely measured from the landscape plan without additional detail. Shrub species shown on plant list (Texas Sage, Dwarf Wax Myrtle, Dwarf Palmetto) appear appropriate for utility clearance. However, the exact spacing and positioning of shrubs relative to transformer access doors should be verified during final plan review.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows shrub symbols throughout the site. Shrub list (Sheet 35) specifies Texas Sage, Dwarf Wax Myrtle, Dwarf Palmetto, and Muhly species with spacing requirements (3' O.C. and 'SEE PLANS'). Exact positioning relative to transformer access door sides cannot be precisely determined from plan view.","reasoning":"While the plant species appear appropriate for utility clearance, the specific positioning of shrubs relative to the 10-foot (access door side) and 5-foot (other sides) clearance requirements cannot be verified without detailed measurement or additional documentation.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Tree locations within 20 feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows proposed trees on site, but specific root barrier details are not provided on any sheet. The requirement specifies root barriers must be minimum 4 feet deep and installed 5 feet from underground electric equipment. No detail sheets show root barrier construction specifications, dimensions, or installation methods for trees within 20 feet of transformer pads.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree locations. Plant list (Sheet 35) confirms proposed tree species. However, no root barrier detail sheets or specifications are provided on any of the submitted plan sheets or supplementary documents.","reasoning":"While the requirement is potentially applicable to proposed trees, the plans do not include root barrier detail drawings or specifications demonstrating compliance with the minimum 4-foot depth and 5-foot offset requirements.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dumpsters or trash enclosures are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan found no dumpster or trash collection areas positioned adjacent to any transformer pad.","reasoning":"This requirement only applies when dumpsters are present adjacent to transformer pads. No such features are shown on the site plan.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No bike racks are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on the site plan. Bike parking is provided elsewhere on the site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan and Sheet 22 (bicycle parking details) found no bike racks positioned adjacent to transformer pads.","reasoning":"This requirement only applies when bike racks are present adjacent to transformer pads. No such proximity exists on the site plan.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No light poles are shown adjacent to or immediately next to transformer pad locations on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan found no light pole callouts positioned adjacent to transformer pads.","reasoning":"This requirement only applies when light poles are adjacent to transformer pads. No such features are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire lanes are designated on the site plan. Fire Lane Plan (Sheet 10) was reviewed and shows no fire lane striping or designations adjacent to transformer pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan) and overall site plan found no designated fire lanes adjacent to transformer pads.","reasoning":"This requirement only applies when fire lanes are designated adjacent to transformer pads. No such designations are shown on the plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Five transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan. They are distributed across the site and have minimum separations of approximately 10.5 to 96.7 feet from each other, all exceeding the 5-foot minimum clearance between transformer pads.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows five discrete transformer pad locations spaced throughout the site with substantial separations between them.","reasoning":"All transformer pads are separated by distances greater than 5 feet, so this requirement is satisfied. No deficiency exists.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water line routing and transformer pad locations are shown on separate sheets (Sheet 19 for utility plan, Sheet 21 for electrical plan). Specific horizontal clearance measurements between transformer pads and water service lines are not annotated. Applicant must verify or provide documentation that all transformer pads maintain minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from water service lines per UCM § 2.9.1.B.2.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) shows water line routing. Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer locations. However, no specific clearance dimensions are annotated between transformer pads and water lines on either sheet.","reasoning":"While both elements are shown on the submitted plans, the specific clearance verification cannot be definitively determined without dimensional annotations or detailed overlay measurements.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wastewater line routing and transformer pad locations are shown on separate sheets. Specific horizontal clearance measurements between transformer pads and wastewater service lines are not annotated. Applicant must verify or provide documentation that all transformer pads maintain minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from wastewater service lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 shows wastewater infrastructure. Sheet 21 shows transformer pads. However, specific clearance dimensions are not annotated between these elements.","reasoning":"While both elements are present on the plans, explicit clearance verification cannot be determined from the submitted drawings without dimensional annotations.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Storm drain line routing and transformer pad locations are shown on separate sheets. Specific horizontal clearance measurements between transformer pads and storm drain lines are not annotated. Applicant must verify or provide documentation that all transformer pads maintain minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from storm drain lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Storm sewer infrastructure is shown on Sheet 12 (Storm Sewer Plan) and transformer locations on Sheet 21. However, specific clearance dimensions are not provided between transformer pads and storm drain infrastructure.","reasoning":"While both elements are present on the submitted plans, specific clearance verification cannot be definitively determined without dimensional annotations or detailed overlay analysis.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas service lines are shown on the utility plan (Sheet 19) or referenced in utility specifications. If gas service is not provided to this property, this requirement is not applicable. However, if gas service is present, clearance documentation would be required. The presence or absence of gas service must be confirmed from utility master plans or Austin Energy Records.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 19) shows water, wastewater, and storm drain infrastructure. No gas lines or gas service references are shown or noted on any submitted plan or supplementary document.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when gas service is present. Without confirmation of gas service existence, applicability cannot be determined from the submitted materials alone.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations and other utility locations are shown on separate sheets without annotated clearance dimensions. Minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearance from transformer pads to other underground utilities (except gas, fuel, steam) is required. Applicant must provide documented verification of clearances to all utilities including electric service lines, conduits, water lines, wastewater lines, and storm drain infrastructure.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows transformer locations on Sheet 21. Utility infrastructure is shown on Sheets 12, 19, and 20. However, no specific 12-inch clearance dimensions are annotated between transformer pads and other utilities.","reasoning":"While utility routing is depicted, specific clearance verification to underground utilities cannot be definitively determined from plan view without detailed dimensional annotations or an overlay analysis.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans show transformer pads, underground utilities, and buildings on multiple sheets. Cross-reference between sheets must be verified to confirm that no transformer pads or AE underground facilities are positioned over/under other utility lines, and that no customer buildings, foundations, or structures are installed over AE underground facilities. Specific documentation or notes confirming clearance verification are not provided on submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows transformer pads and underground electric routing. Utility plans show water, wastewater, and storm drain facilities. Building locations are shown on site and electrical plans. However, no notes or documentation confirm that cross-utility conflicts have been analyzed and verified.","reasoning":"While all relevant features are depicted on the submitted plans, specific verification documentation that no conflicts exist is not provided. Cross-utility coordination documentation would be necessary to verify compliance.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution lines are shown on the electrical plan (Sheet 21) or utility plan (Sheet 19). Landscape plan shows reference to 'OHE' (Overhead Electric) on Sheet 31. If overhead distribution lines are not present on this property, this requirement is not applicable. However, if overhead lines exist, the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance must be documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) and Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 19) do not indicate the presence of overhead distribution conductors. Landscape plan references 'OHE' on the plan legend but this may refer to existing external overhead lines.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when overhead distribution lines are present. The status cannot be definitively determined from the submitted plans without clarification on whether overhead service is planned or existing.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors are clearly identified as present on this property. Landscape plan references 'OHE' but the presence of primary/neutral distribution conductors (as distinguished from secondary service lines) is not documented. If overhead distribution conductors are not present, this requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) and utility plans do not explicitly show overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors. If overhead lines exist on adjacent property, they would be external to this site.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when overhead distribution primary/neutral conductors are present on or immediately adjacent to the property. The submitted plans do not clearly document such presence.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Niche service is a specialized installation where transformer equipment is accessible from outside but located within the customer's building footprint. Site plan shows all five transformer pads located outside building footprints in open areas. No niche configurations (enclosed or notched-out building areas) are proposed on this site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and electrical plan show all five transformer pads positioned in open areas outside building footprints - west of Buildings 1, 2, and 8, and between building pairs (Bldgs 4-5 and Bldgs 7-6).","reasoning":"Niche service requirements only apply when equipment is located within building footprints (accessible from outside). All proposed transformer pads are located outside buildings in open areas, so this requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installations are proposed. All transformer pads are located in open areas outside building footprints.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site and electrical plans confirm all transformer pads are in open areas outside building footprints.","reasoning":"Niche fire wall rating requirements only apply when niche service is proposed (equipment within building footprint). No niche configurations exist on this site plan.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (survey requirement as required by AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["Areas around all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances in access paths above or adjacent to transformer pad locations. This is required when overhead structures, parking garages, enclosed areas, or niches are present above or adjacent to transformer locations. The absence of cross-section drawings prevents verification of vertical clearance compliance for any structures that might exist above the transformer access areas.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of all 39 plan sheets found no cross-section drawings specifically documenting vertical clearances above transformer pad locations. Sheets 17 (Conveyance Cross Sections), 38-39 (Wall Details), and others show cross-sections but not for transformer access areas.","reasoning":"Cross-section drawings may be required by AE Design to document vertical clearance compliance. The absence of such drawings means vertical clearance above transformer access paths cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on the electrical plan or any supplementary documents. Grading plan does not show transformer pad locations or drainage flow directions around them. The requirement to slope drainage away from buildings applies only to oil-filled equipment. Without equipment type specification and grading details at transformer pads, compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) does not specify equipment type. Grading plan (Sheet 11) does not show transformer pad locations or drainage flow patterns at those locations. No AE Design equipment specifications provided.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to oil-filled transformer equipment and requires grading analysis at the transformer pad. Both the equipment type specification and the detailed grading at transformer location are absent from submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision measurements on Sheet 9 confirm that all transformer pads are located on private property with substantial clearances from right-of-way and property boundaries. Western transformer pads are 21.2 feet and 61.2 feet from the western ROW boundary. Central transformer pads are distributed across the private property interior. All transformer pads are 100% on private property and do not encroach into public right-of-way.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement confirmed western transformer pads have 21.2 and 61.2 feet clearance from ROW boundary. Site plan shows all transformer pads interior to property boundaries.","reasoning":"All measured distances confirm transformer pads are on private property with clear separation from ROW. No transformer pads are located in public right-of-way or straddling property lines.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4 (property requirement); easement-specific regulations"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plat sheet (Sheet 2) shows various easements on the property including drainage easements, public utility easements, and electric easements. Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations. However, specific documentation confirming that transformer pads are NOT located within drainage easements, water easements, sewer easements, or electrical easements (without AE Design written approval) is not provided. Applicant must verify that no transformer pads encroach into prohibited easement areas or provide written Austin Energy Design approval for any permitted encroachments.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 2 depicts multiple easements on the property. Sheet 21 shows transformer locations. However, no notes or documentation confirm that transformer pad locations have been verified against the easement footprints and that no conflicts exist.","reasoning":"While both easement and transformer pad locations are shown on submitted plans, explicit verification documentation that no prohibited easement conflicts exist is not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (additional clearance and access easements may be required)"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations but does not identify or dimension any transformer easements. Austin Energy Design determines the width and configuration of transformer easements based on equipment specifications, access requirements, and maintenance clearances. No transformer easement specifications, widths, or documentation from Austin Energy Design are provided on the submitted plans. Applicant must obtain transformer easement requirements from Austin Energy Design and depict them on the site plan with appropriate dimensions and recorded easement documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows transformer pad symbols but includes no callouts or dimensions for transformer easements. No easement exhibit or documentation from Austin Energy Design is included in the submittal.","reasoning":"AE Design determines transformer easement requirements on a project-specific basis. The plans do not show these easements or include AE Design approval documentation.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical service routing from all transformer pads to building meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electric line routing from transformer pads, but specific documentation confirming that all electrical routing from transformers to building meters is 100% on private property is not provided. Applicant must provide notes or documentation confirming that no electrical service lines cross public right-of-way or encroach into easements controlled by third parties.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows electric routing lines from transformer pads to buildings, but no notes confirm that routing is 100% on private property throughout.","reasoning":"While the electrical routing is depicted on the plan, specific documentation or notes verifying compliance with the 100% private property requirement is not included.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0 (obtain transformer pad detail from AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad symbols but does not provide dimensions, specifications, or a reference to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets. Transformer pad dimensions and construction details must match AE Design-approved specifications for the specified service type (single-phase or three-phase). Service type is also not specified on the electrical plans. Applicant must obtain the ESPA (Electric Service Planning Application) from Austin Energy and the corresponding AE Design-approved transformer pad details, then depict or reference these details on the plan set with confirmed service type.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows transformer pad location symbols but no dimensions or specifications. Supplementary documents do not include ESPA or AE Design transformer pad detail sheets. Service type (single-phase vs. three-phase) is not specified.","reasoning":"AE Design provides project-specific transformer pad details based on the service type and electrical load. These approved details are required to be shown or referenced on the plans to verify pad dimensions. The submitted plans do not include these specifications or approvals.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads are located more than 4 feet away from parking areas and vehicle circulation routes. The closest transformer pad to parking/traffic is 15.9 feet away. Therefore, the 4-inch diameter bollard requirement does not apply, as no transformer pads fall within the 4-foot trigger distance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements on Sheet 21 measured distances from all five transformer pads to nearest parking areas and drive lanes. Minimum distance found was 15.9 feet (transformer east of Bldg. 7 to nearest drive lane).","reasoning":"The bollard requirement is gated by the 4-foot proximity trigger. Since all transformer pads are more than 4 feet from parking/traffic areas, this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution facilities are clearly identified as present on or immediately above this property on the electrical plan. Landscape plan references 'OHE' (Overhead Electric) but the presence of customer-installed structures (buildings, parking garages, light poles, signs, billboards, chimneys, antennas, tanks) under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities cannot be definitively assessed without clarification on whether overhead distribution conductors serve this property.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical and utility plans do not clearly identify overhead distribution conductors as present on this site. If overhead service exists, its location and spatial relationship to proposed site features would need to be confirmed.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when overhead distribution facilities are present. The submitted plans do not clearly document whether overhead distribution serves this property.","tools_used":[]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2088,"cache_read_input_tokens":75249,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2088},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_t