{"level":30,"time":1778524312359,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CViB4jAn1Nu4UU7cQKpqCd","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided site plan, there are specific electric easements labeled, and there are proposed improvements that appear to fall within these areas. \n\nHere are the exact details found on the plan:\n\n**Electric Easements Identified:**\n1.  **Eastern Boundary (Right side of the plan):** There is a label that reads exactly **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** pointing to a 5-foot dashed setback line running parallel to the eastern property boundary.\n2.  **Southern Boundary (Bottom of the plan):** There is a label that reads exactly **\"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** pointing to a 5-foot dashed setback line running parallel to the southern property line.\n3.  **Southeast Corner (Bottom right):** There is a label that reads exactly **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"** pointing toward the easement lines at the property corner.\n\n**Encroachments / Improvements within the Easements:**\n*   **Concrete Retaining Wall:** A continuous heavy solid line labeled **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"** runs along both the southern and eastern property boundaries. \n*   Along the **southern boundary**, this proposed retaining wall is drawn in the narrow strip directly between the outer property line and the inner 5-foot dashed easement line, meaning it falls entirely within the \"5' Elec. Easement\".\n*   Along the **eastern boundary**, the plan notes an **\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\"** and shows the new wall alignment running along or immediately inside the property line, which places it within the \"5' Electric Easement\".\n*   The primary buildings (such as Bldg 5, Bldg 6, Bldg 7, and Bldg 8), sidewalks, and driveways appear to be set back and do not encroach into these specific 5-foot electric easement strips, but the retaining walls clearly do."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bdd8a02-49ee-4d1f-8b8c-60e98c23c29e","uuid":"30a6d3c2-2cc3-4652-9617-5a5976527cd9","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided site plan, there are specific electric easements labeled, and there are proposed improvements that appear to fall within these areas. \n\nHere are the exact details found on the plan:\n\n**Electric Easements Identified:**\n1.  **Eastern Boundary (Right side of the plan):** There is a label that reads exactly **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** pointing to a 5-foot dashed setback line running parallel to the eastern property boundary.\n2.  **Southern Boundary (Bottom of the plan):** There is a label that reads exactly **\"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** pointing to a 5-foot dashed setback line running parallel to the southern property line.\n3.  **Southeast Corner (Bottom right):** There is a label that reads exactly **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"** pointing toward the easement lines at the property corner.\n\n**Encroachments / Improvements within the Easements:**\n*   **Concrete Retaining Wall:** A continuous heavy solid line labeled **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"** runs along both the southern and eastern property boundaries. \n*   Along the **southern boundary**, this proposed retaining wall is drawn in the narrow strip directly between the outer property line and the inner 5-foot dashed easement line, meaning it falls entirely within the \"5' Elec. Easement\".\n*   Along the **eastern boundary**, the plan notes an **\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\"** and shows the new wall alignment running along or immediately inside the property line, which places it within the \"5' Electric Easemen