{"level":30,"time":1778524433031,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_015RPAhpDdFmAfk9CZy3a8nV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've completed the structured output with all findings. Now let me provide a summary for the user.\n\nBased on my review, I found:\n\n**FAIL items (4):**\n1. EL-1.7 - Missing building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations\n2. EL-1.8 - Missing section/plan view clearance dimension annotations\n3. EL-1.14 - Retaining walls encroach within electric easements\n4. EL-1.17 - Wall detail sections lack clearance verification dimensions\n5. EL-1.23 - No clearance dimensions shown; measurement methodology not documented\n6. EL-1.27 - Retaining walls within electric easement violate prohibition on structures in easements  \n7. EL-1.31 - No registered surveyor mid-span clearance data provided\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE items (6):**\n1. EL-1.2 - Cannot verify 15-foot radial clearance (voltage not specified)\n2. EL-1.6 - Cannot verify buildings in ROW clearances (utility status ambiguous)\n3. EL-1.12 - Cannot verify transmission line fencing (voltage not specified)\n4. EL-1.18 - Cannot verify vertical clearance to driveways (no conductor elevation survey)\n5. EL-1.20 - Cannot verify transmission line vertical clearance (voltage not specified)\n6. EL-1.25 - Cannot verify sidewalk clearance from poles (exact positions not dimensioned)\n7. EL-1.37 - Cannot verify tree species compliance (trees not identified by species on landscape plan)\n8. EL-1.40 - Cannot verify down guy conflicts (guy locations not depicted)\n9. EL-1.42 - Cannot verify down guy anchor easements (locations not shown)\n\n**PASS items (2):**\n1. EL-1.1 - Buildings maintain adequate clearance (26-68.9 feet exceed 7.5-foot minimum)\n\n\n2. EL-1.46 - 48-hour notification note found on Sheet 3\n\nThe core issues are that overhead electric lines appear on the plans but lack voltage designation, making clearance verification impossible. Retaining walls positioned within electric easements represent a significant violation. Additionally, no clearance dimensions are documented for any OHE facilities, building elevations are absent, and trees near lines aren't identified by species. The most serious deficiency involves retaining walls encroaching the electric easement, which directly violates easement restrictions on structures.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11953,"cache_read_input_tokens":75786,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11953},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bdd8a02-49ee-4d1f-8b8c-60e98c23c29e","uuid":"1025f3da-2da2-4a39-8060-1411403d3324"}
{"level":30,"time":1778524441440,"pid":86444,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_015RPAhpDdFmAfk9CZy3a8nV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Site Plan Review Summary: Grouping 1 - Overhead Electric Line Clearances\n\nI have completed the site plan review for the **Valley View Townhomes** project against the **Overhead Electric Line Clearances** grouping (Austin LDC/Energy Code requirements).\n\n### KEY FINDINGS\n\n**Overhead Electric Infrastructure Identified:**\n- Overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on Site Plan (Sheet 9) and Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)\n- Two routing branches: southern boundary (south of Building 8) and eastern boundary (east of Buildings 5 & 6)\n- 5-foot Electric Easements documented for both boundaries per county plat records\n- **Voltage classification NOT specified** (critical gap - cannot determine if distribution or transmission)\n\n### CRITICAL DEFICIENCIES FOUND (7 FAIL + 9 NOT-VERIFIABLE)\n\n**Major Issues:**\n\n1. **Retaining Walls in Electric Easements (EL-1.14, EL-1.27)** ⚠️\n   - Proposed retaining walls drawn WITHIN the 5-foot Electric Easement boundaries\n   - Violates prohibition on structures within utility easements\n   - No clearance dimensions from conductor to wall shown\n   - Must be relocated outside easements OR require Austin Energy written authorization\n\n2. **Missing Clearance Dimensions (EL-1.8, EL-1.23)**\n   - No dimension annotations showing distance from outer conductor to buildings/structures\n   - Measurement methodology (conductor vs. pole centerline) not documented\n   - Required per UCM § 1.10.3 for compliance verification\n\n3. **Missing Building Elevation Sheets (EL-1.7)**\n   - No building elevation sheets in 39-sheet package\n   - Surveyed overhead conductor elevations not shown\n   - Required to verify vertical clearances to building projections\n\n4. **No Mid-Span Clearance Survey (EL-1.31)**\n   - No registered surveyor data showing conductor elevations\n   - Vertical clearance to driveways cannot be verified\n   - Required for facilities with marginal clearances\n\n5. **Voltage Classification Ambiguous (EL-1.2, EL-1.12, EL-1.20, EL-1.37)**\n   - OHE lines not labeled with voltage (12.47kV, 34.5kV, 69kV, 138kV, etc.)\n   - Cannot verify if lines are distribution or transmission\n   - Cannot confirm which clearance standards apply (10-ft vs. 50-ft tree distance, voltage-specific clearances)\n\n6. **Trees Near OHE Not Identified (EL-1.37)**\n   - Mitigation trees (M symbols) shown 0.5-72 feet from OHE line\n   - Species not documented on landscape plan for trees within clearance zones\n   - Cannot verify Utility Compatible (UC) species compliance per ECM Appendix F\n\n### ISSUES THAT PASSED\n\n✓ **EL-1.1:** Buildings maintain adequate clearance\n   - Building 8: 26 feet from southern OHE\n   - Building 5: 68.9 feet from eastern OHE  \n   - Building 6: 18.9 feet from eastern OHE\n   - All exceed 7.5-foot minimum\n\n✓ **EL-1.46:** 48-hour notification note present\n   - Sheet 3 contains Austin Energy pre-construction safety meeting requirement\n\n### APPLICABILITY NOTE\n\nPer the Applicability Gate Principle: **This grouping is applicable** to the project because:\n- Overhead electric facilities exist on/adjacent to site (OHE lines shown on plans)\n- Multiple proposed site features exist (buildings, retaining walls, driveways, landscaping)\n- Clearance requirements are mandatory when facilities coexist\n\n---\n\n**Recommendation:** Applicant must submit revised plans addressing:\n1. Relocate retaining walls outside 5-foot electric easements OR obtain Austin Energy easement authorization\n2. Add clearance dimension annotations from outer conductor to all structures\n3. Provide building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations\n4. Submit registered surveyor mid-span clearance data for vertical clearance verification\n5. Clarify voltage classification of OHE lines (distribution vs. transmission)\n6. Identify tree species on landscape plan for all trees within 10-50 feet of OHE lines"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11953,"cache_read_input_tokens":75786,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11953},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bdd8a02-49ee-4d1f-8b8c-60e98c23c29e","uuid":"61c19a04-88c3-47ab-a9a7-de3df0b64ca4"}
