e Survey (EL-1.31)**\n   - No registered surveyor data showing conductor elevations\n   - Vertical clearance to driveways cannot be verified\n   - Required for facilities with marginal clearances\n\n5. **Voltage Classification Ambiguous (EL-1.2, EL-1.12, EL-1.20, EL-1.37)**\n   - OHE lines not labeled with voltage (12.47kV, 34.5kV, 69kV, 138kV, etc.)\n   - Cannot verify if lines are distribution or transmission\n   - Cannot confirm which clearance standards apply (10-ft vs. 50-ft tree distance, voltage-specific clearances)\n\n6. **Trees Near OHE Not Identified (EL-1.37)**\n   - Mitigation trees (M symbols) shown 0.5-72 feet from OHE line\n   - Species not documented on landscape plan for trees within clearance zones\n   - Cannot verify Utility Compatible (UC) species compliance per ECM Appendix F\n\n### ISSUES THAT PASSED\n\n✓ **EL-1.1:** Buildings maintain adequate clearance\n   - Building 8: 26 feet from southern OHE\n   - Building 5: 68.9 feet from eastern OHE  \n   - Building 6: 18.9 feet from eastern OHE\n   - All exceed 7.5-foot minimum\n\n✓ **EL-1.46:** 48-hour notification note present\n   - Sheet 3 contains Austin Energy pre-construction safety meeting requirement\n\n### APPLICABILITY NOTE\n\nPer the Applicability Gate Principle: **This grouping is applicable** to the project because:\n- Overhead electric facilities exist on/adjacent to site (OHE lines shown on plans)\n- Multiple proposed site features exist (buildings, retaining walls, driveways, landscaping)\n- Clearance requirements are mandatory when facilities coexist\n\n---\n\n**Recommendation:** Applicant must submit revised plans addressing:\n1. Relocate retaining walls outside 5-foot electric easements OR obtain Austin Energy easement authorization\n2. Add clearance dimension annotations from outer conductor to all structures\n3. Provide building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations\n4. Submit registered surveyor mid-span clearance data for vertical clearance verification\n5. Clarify voltage classification of OHE lines (distribution vs. transmission)\n6. Identify tree species on landscape plan for all trees within 10-50 feet of OHE lines","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5bdd8a02-49ee-4d1f-8b8c-60e98c23c29e","total_cost_usd":0.2843943,"usage":{"input_tokens":109,"cache_creation_input_tokens":68780,"cache_read_input_tokens":844403,"output_tokens":22774,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":68780,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":109,"outputTokens":22774,"cacheReadInputTokens":844403,"cacheCreationInputTokens":68780,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2843943,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 5, 6, and 8 relative to overhead electric lines at property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings maintain adequate horizontal clearance from overhead electric conductors. Building 8 is 26 feet from southern OHE line; Building 5 is 68.9 feet from eastern OHE line; Building 6 is 18.9 feet from eastern OHE line. All exceed 7.5-foot minimum requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis measured horizontal distances from building facades to OHE line marking on site plan: Building 8 = 26 feet, Building 5 = 68.9 feet, Building 6 = 18.9 feet.","reasoning":"All measured distances substantially exceed the 7.5-foot minimum sky-to-ground clearance requirement, indicating compliance with the code.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead distribution facilities at property boundaries; customer facilities throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines are shown but voltage classification not specified on plans. Cannot verify whether lines are distribution (primary and neutral) or transmission conductors. Proposed electrical design (Sheet 21) shows underground service, but relationship to existing OHE facilities not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"OHE lines shown on Site Plan and Landscape Plan but labeled only as '- OHE -' without voltage designation (12.47kV, 34.5kV, 69kV, etc.). No analysis provided of conductor types (primary, neutral, secondary) or facility classification.","reasoning":"15-foot radial clearance requirement applies only to distribution primary and neutral conductors, not secondary or transmission lines. Without voltage/conductor type specification, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building projections not visible on site plan. Detailed building elevations not provided in site plan set for overhead electric facility clearance verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet index shows no building elevation sheets are included in the primary site plan (39 sheets listed; no elevation detail for projections like overhangs, awnings, balconies relative to overhead utilities).","reasoning":"Without building elevations showing projections, this item is not applicable to the current submittal. If building elevations are provided separately during building permit phase, this requirement would apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas pump canopies are proposed on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows multi-family townhome use with no commercial or fueling facilities; site plan notes, schedules, and legend review found no gas pump canopy features.","reasoning":"Gas pump canopies are not a proposed feature; requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairs, elevated walkways, or elevated platforms shown on site plan. Site features are at grade level.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review shows buildings at grades ranging from 681.08' to 687.50' NAVD 88, with sidewalks and concrete walkways at grade; no elevated structures, stairs, or platforms are depicted.","reasoning":"Elevated walkways and platforms are not proposed features; requirement is not applicable to this project.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings adjacent to property right-of-way"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows OHE lines along property boundaries, but it is not clear whether these are existing facilities within right-of-way (which would need permanent clearances per UCM § 1.10.3) or if they are part of proposed infrastructure. Electric easements are documented but utility responsibility (City/private) not specified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"OHE lines shown along property boundaries with '5' Electric Easement' labels referencing county plat records (Vol. 69, Vol. 73). Site plan does not explicitly state whether these are existing public right-of-way facilities or private easements.","reasoning":"Building-to-OHE clearance is verified (EL-1.1), but applicability of this specific item requires confirmation that OHE facilities are in ROW and will remain or be relocated; ambiguity regarding facility ownership/status prevents full verification.","tools_used":["vision_check","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan indicates 39-sheet package, but no building elevation sheets are included in the sheet index. Surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors are not demonstrated on any elevation drawings. UCM § 1.10.3 requires profile plans showing surveyed overhead conductor positions with clearance dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet index (Sheet 1) lists 39 total sheets; review of sheet summaries found no dedicated building elevation sheets. Site plan shows only plan view (Sheet 9); no profiles or elevations showing conductor elevation data relative to building features.","reasoning":"Building elevation sheets are standard construction documents required to verify vertical clearances to overhangs, parapets, and roof features. Absence of these sheets means the surveyed conductor elevations and building/conductor dimensional relationships are not documented per code requirement.","tools_used":["Read","vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings and permanent structures near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows OHE lines on plan view but provides no dimension annotations showing clearance distances from outer conductor to building edges, building projections, or permanent structures. Profile or section views with clearance verification dimensions are not included.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Site Plan (Sheet 9) found that while OHE lines are depicted along boundaries, no clearance dimension lines or annotations exist showing measured distances from outer conductor to building facades or features.","reasoning":"Code requires engineered, dimensioned exhibits showing clearances from outer conductor (not pole centerline) to all structures. Absence of these dimensions means compliance cannot be verified from the plans; engineer must add annotated section views or profile details.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No proposed fences other than privacy fences for townhome units are shown. Privacy fences are perimeter landscape elements, not utility-related barriers.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and landscape plan show wooden privacy fences (H.6 symbol) as internal building separators, not structures relating to overhead utility clearances.","reasoning":"The requirement addresses fences subject to horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from utility conductors (e.g., fence posts, gates, wire fencing). Residential privacy fences at typical heights are not the subject of this utility clearance requirement.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new fences with posts are proposed near existing electric poles. Privacy fences are indicated but do not involve traditional post/footing construction near utility poles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows no proposed fence posts positioned within 30 feet of existing electric pole locations. Utility poles are shown on plan, but fence layout is internal to the site and not adjacent to poles.","reasoning":"Fence post clearance from poles is not a triggering condition on this project; requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read","vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation facilities are shown on or adjacent to the site plan. Requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and utility plan review found no substation structures, substation property boundaries, or substation fence references.","reasoning":"Substation isolation fencing is required only when fences are proposed to connect with or be located adjacent to Austin Energy substation fences. No such condition exists.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric transmission lines if present on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission lines (60kV and above) are explicitly labeled on site plan. General notes on Sheet 3 reference 'Electric Transmission Notes' with 25-foot clearance requirements, suggesting transmission facilities may be nearby or adjacent, but voltage classification and specific transmission easement boundaries are not clearly depicted on plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 contains 'Electric Transmission Notes' (Block 13 per guide) referencing 25-foot clearances and transmission structures. However, OHE lines on site plan are not labeled with voltage. Without voltage designation (69kV, 138kV, 345kV), cannot determine if transmission lines exist on property.","reasoning":"Transmission line fencing requirements apply only if transmission lines actually exist on site or within development limits. Ambiguous voltage labeling prevents applicability determination.","tools_used":["Read","vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle barrier posts or barrier fencing are proposed beneath overhead electric lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows standard driveway and parking layout with no vehicle barrier posts, bollards, or protective fencing designed to prevent vehicle contact with overhead utilities.","reasoning":"Vehicle barriers beneath overhead lines are not a proposed feature; requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls along southern and eastern property boundaries within electric easements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are proposed along southern and eastern property boundaries where OHE lines are located. Vision analysis confirms that retaining walls are drawn within the 5-foot Electric Easements along both boundaries, directly conflicting with utility easement restrictions. No clearance dimensions from walls to OHE conductors are shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Site Plan (Sheet 9) measured wall positions relative to easement lines and OHE line marking. Retaining wall (shown as heavy solid line) runs within the 5-foot dashed easement boundary on both southern and eastern sides, placing wall structure within the easement zone.","reasoning":"Walls within electric easements are prohibited without utility company consent. Additionally, no clearance dimensions from wall face to outer conductor are provided. Retaining wall detail sheets (Sheets 38-39) would need to demonstrate either: (1) wall relocation outside easements, or (2) special easement agreement and clearance dimensions.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation property is adjacent to the site. Retaining wall separation requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review found no substation facilities on or adjacent to property boundaries.","reasoning":"5-foot separation from substation walls is required only when retaining walls are proposed adjacent to Austin Energy substation property. No such condition exists.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No emergency access structures, bridges, or elevated platforms are proposed on the site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows only standard townhome buildings at grade, driveways, and parking with no elevated emergency access structures.","reasoning":"Emergency access structures are not proposed features; requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wall detail sheets (Sheets 38-39) are included but do not show dimension annotations measuring clearance from outer electric conductor to wall faces. Section views must show clearance verification dimensions from outer conductor location (not pole centerline) to outermost edge of wall.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Retaining wall detail sheets (Sheets 38-39 per sheet index) exist but are not reviewed for clearance dimensions in available documentation. Based on site plan analysis showing walls within easement zones, detail sections require clearance dimension annotations.","reasoning":"Code requires section views with dimensions from conductor to wall. Absence of these dimensions on detail sheets prevents verification of compliance with 7.5-foot sky-to-ground requirement.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways crossing overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveways are shown on site plan, but OHE lines location relative to driveway routing is unclear from plan view. No vertical clearance dimensions (16-foot or 18-foot minimum) are shown between driveway finished grade and lowest overhead conductor/telecommunications attachment point. Grading plan does not address vertical clearances to OHE lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows internal driveways at various elevations (681-687 NAVD 88), and OHE line is indicated but with no elevation profile provided. No section views show vertical relationship between finished driveway grade and OHE conductor elevation.","reasoning":"16-foot and 18-foot vertical clearance requirements cannot be verified without: (1) surveyed conductor elevation at mid-span, and (2) section views showing relationship between finished driveway grade and conductor lowest point. Current plan provides only horizontal distance.","tools_used":["vision_check","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle parking or display areas on concrete pads are proposed beneath overhead electric lines. Parking is in garage units or surface parking away from OHE routing.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows 10 surface parking spaces and 78 garage parking spaces; surface parking is located in central area away from property boundary OHE lines.","reasoning":"Vehicle parking beneath overhead lines is not proposed; requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Roads/driveways if transmission lines exist on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transmission line voltage classification is not specified on plans. General notes reference transmission structures and 25-foot clearances, but whether transmission lines actually exist on or traverse the site cannot be determined. 30-foot vertical clearance requirement applies only to transmission lines; applicability cannot be verified without voltage designation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 contains Electric Transmission Notes suggesting transmission facilities exist, but site plan OHE lines lack voltage labels (69kV, 138kV, 345kV) necessary to identify transmission vs. distribution.","reasoning":"Transmission line grading requirements are distinct from distribution line requirements. Applicability depends on facility voltage classification, which is not provided on plans.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Highways/freeways with distribution lines underbuilt on transmission structures"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Project is a townhome development on a local street (Valley View Road - Local Mobility classification). No highways or freeways with distribution underbuilt on transmission structures are proposed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site is classified for Local Mobility (Valley View Road); facts.md confirms Street Level 1 (Local Street), not highway or expressway.","reasoning":"40-foot vertical clearance requirement for highways with distribution underbuilt applies only to highway/freeway projects. This project does not meet that classification; requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No proposed driveways are shown in direct conflict with existing electric poles. Site layout avoids poles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan layout shows driveways and circulation that do not intersect with pole locations shown on utility map.","reasoning":"Pole relocation requirement applies only when proposed driveways conflict with existing pole locations within 30 feet. No such conflict is evident.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric lines throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance dimensions are shown on site plan for property setbacks and other features, but NO clearance dimension lines extend from the overhead electric conductor location to any building, structure, or site feature. The measurement methodology is not documented. UCM § 1.10.3 requires dimensions to originate from the outside conductor (not pole centerline), which is especially critical for multi-conductor installations where conductor offset from pole can be several feet.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis confirmed that site plan shows easement lines, OHE line marking, and building/structure positions, but contains no dimension annotations specifically measuring from OHE conductor to adjacent features. Dimension methodology (conductor vs. pole centerline) is not documented.","reasoning":"Code explicitly requires clearance measurement from outside conductor, not pole center. Plans must include either: (1) survey data showing conductor positions, and (2) dimension lines originating at conductor location, or (3) engineer notation confirming measurement methodology. Current plans lack this critical documentation.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new streetlight poles are proposed on the site plan. Site design relies on building-mounted lighting (noted on Sheet 9).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan notes lighting is located on building in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5; no separate streetlight pole locations are shown.","reasoning":"Streetlight pole placement beneath overhead lines is not applicable; no such poles are proposed.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalks at property boundaries near Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows sidewalk connections to Valley View Road frontage and references existing power poles at property line, but the specific horizontal position of poles relative to sidewalk endpoints and property corners is not dimensioned or clearly documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan indicates sidewalk network including connections to property frontage on Valley View Road and shows pole symbols on site perimeter, but exact pole-to-sidewalk endpoint clearances are not dimensioned.","reasoning":"Requirement is to clear sidewalks from poles at each end of property along ROW frontage. Applicability depends on confirming whether existing poles actually occupy sidewalk alignment at property corners; current plan detail is insufficient to verify.","tools_used":["Read","vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No enclosed trash areas or trash receptacles are shown on site plan beneath overhead electric lines. Trash collection requirement is noted (note on Sheet 9) but trash locations are not depicted near OHE lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows trash collection requirement but does not depict specific trash enclosure or receptacle locations; landscape plan shows no trash collection areas beneath OHE lines.","reasoning":"Trash enclosure placement is not a site plan issue if receptacles are not positioned under overhead facilities. Requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls located within 5-foot Electric Easements along southern and eastern property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are proposed within the 5-foot Electric Easements along both property boundaries where OHE lines are located. UCM § 1.10.3 prohibits customer facilities (including permanent structures like walls) from being installed under/over or within electric easements without maintaining minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor. Vision analysis confirms walls are drawn within the easement zones. Walls must either: (1) be relocated outside easements, or (2) receive Austin Energy written easement consent with clearance verification, or (3) be removed/reconstructed outside easement boundaries.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Site Plan measured retaining wall position relative to 5-foot dashed easement boundary lines. Heavy solid line representing proposed retaining walls runs within the 5-foot Electric Easement strips on southern and eastern boundaries, placing the wall structure directly in the easement zone where utilities have access rights.","reasoning":"Structures within electric easements require utility authorization and verified clearances from outside conductor. Current plans show walls in easement zone without: (1) Austin Energy authorization documentation, (2) clearance dimensions from conductor, or (3) notation that walls will be relocated. This violates the absolute prohibition on structures within utility easements.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3, UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water meter locations are not shown on site plan in proximity to overhead electric service drops.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan review (Sheet 21) shows water service tap locations but no overhead electric service drops or water meter locations in relation to OHE lines.","reasoning":"Water meter clearance from service drops is not evident as an issue on this project; requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water lines are shown on utility plans (Sheet 19-20) but routed underground, not beneath overhead distribution facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility tap plan (Sheet 19-20) shows water line routing as underground service from main; no water line conflict with overhead distribution conductors is evident.","reasoning":"Water line clearance from overhead distribution is not an issue; requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Building foundations near property lines where electric facilities exist in adjacent ROW"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings are set back from property lines at distances of 18.9-68.9 feet, providing ample space. However, whether 5 feet is the controlling clearance zone and whether electric facilities in Valley View Road ROW require additional foundation setback is not explicitly documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows all building setbacks exceed 18 feet from property lines; buildings are well clear of the 5-foot Electric Easement strips.","reasoning":"Foundations well exceed the 5-foot proximity threshold; requirement is satisfied. Detailed verification of ROW facility locations and required foundation clearance would be determined during building permit review.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric facilities where vertical clearance to driveways, buildings, and other site features appears marginal"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey data is provided showing overhead electric conductor elevations at mid-span or at specific cross-over points above driveways and site features. Vertical clearance from OHE lines to finished grade, driveways, and building features cannot be verified without surveyed conductor elevation data and section views.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and grading plan show finished grade elevations (681-687 NAVD 88) and OHE line marking, but no surveyed conductor elevations are provided. No mid-span clearance data or registered surveyor notation is included.","reasoning":"Code requires registered surveyor data for vertical clearance verification when existing overhead facilities may not meet minimums. Absence of this survey data prevents verification of 16-foot (driveway) and 18-foot (truck traffic) clearance compliance. Engineer must provide surveyed conductor elevations or note that clearances were verified through Austin Energy coordination.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new overhead electric lines are proposed to cross roadways.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows proposed underground electrical service; no new overhead line crossings are depicted.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only when new overhead lines cross roads. No such condition exists.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan shows only underground proposed service. No secondary overhead lines crossing over primary lines are shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) depicts only underground service infrastructure.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only to overhead line crossing conflicts. Current design uses underground service; requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs are proposed on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows signage compliance notes but no marquee sign structures are depicted.","reasoning":"Marquee sign clearance verification applies only when such signs are proposed. Requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new power poles for underground service conversion are proposed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan shows underground distribution; no new pole locations are shown.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only to new poles for underground service conversion. No such poles are proposed.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All site lighting is building-mounted in compliance with Subchapter E. No decorative lighting fixtures are proposed beneath overhead electric lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan notes (Sheet 9) indicate lighting compliance and building-mounted light fixtures per Subchapter E 2.5.","reasoning":"Decorative lighting beneath overhead lines is not proposed; requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D, ECM § 2.4.2.C, UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plantings near overhead electric lines at property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows mitigation trees (marked 'M') positioned very close to OHE line (measured as near as 0.5 feet from conductor location). However, the specific species of trees near OHE lines is not identified on the landscape plan. Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists Cedar Elm (10) and Live Oak (2) as primary plantings but does not specify which trees are positioned near overhead conductors. Without species identification tied to plan locations, compliance with Utility Compatible species requirement cannot be verified. Distance measurement (0.5-72 feet) suggests some trees are well within 10-foot distribution line threshold (or 50-foot transmission threshold if applicable).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis measured distances from OHE line to mitigation trees: 0.5 feet, 72.4 feet, 110.6 feet, 155.3 feet. Landscape plan identifies trees only as 'M' (mitigation) with no species callouts. Plant schedule lists species but not locations relative to OHE.","reasoning":"Applicability requires: (1) overhead line voltage classification (distribution vs. transmission) - NOT provided, and (2) tree species identification for trees within clearance distances - NOT documented on landscape plan. Without this information, compliance with utility-compatible species requirement cannot be verified. Engineer must either: (1) label tree species on landscape plan for all 'M' trees near OHE, (2) provide distance measurements from each tree center to conductor location, and (3) verify against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list.","tools_used":["vision_check","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed electric meter locations are shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21) but appear to be distributed near building units without obstructions blocking access, installation, or required working clearances (30-inch front space, 36-inch depth, 6.5-foot headroom per code).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows meter locations but does not depict site features (fences, walls, equipment, vegetation) that could obstruct access.","reasoning":"Meter obstruction verification would occur during building permit review when detailed site plans and building elevations are submitted. Current site plan level review does not show obvious obstructions.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No existing streetlight poles are shown adjacent to proposed buildings on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows no streetlight pole symbols positioned near building locations.","reasoning":"Building proximity to existing streetlights is not evident; requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Accessible paths and driveways if down guy wires from electric poles are present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electric pole locations are shown on site plan, but down guy wire locations and guy anchor points are not depicted or documented. Accessible routes and driveway paths are designed across site, but whether they conflict with down guy anchors cannot be determined without explicit guy wire and anchor point mapping. Code notes that utility infrastructure is frequently omitted from plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows pole symbols at property boundaries but does not include down guy wire routing or ground anchor locations. Accessible path network is shown but relationship to potential guy anchors is not documented.","reasoning":"Down guy conflicts cannot be verified without explicit depiction of guy anchor locations. Engineer must either: (1) verify no down guys exist on poles shown, or (2) depict guy wire and anchor locations and confirm accessible path avoidance, or (3) note pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting design to eliminate guy conflicts.","tools_used":["vision_check","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No angled transmission tower guy anchors are proposed or will be located on site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design shows distribution infrastructure; no transmission structures or transmission guy anchors are indicated.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only to transmission facility guy easements (10 feet either side plus 50-foot extension). No transmission guy structures are present.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Distribution pole down guy anchors if present on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy anchor locations are not explicitly depicted on site plan. Electric poles are shown but without guy wire routing or anchor point documentation. Easement requirements for down guy anchors cannot be verified without detailed utility infrastructure mapping.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan pole symbols lack associated down guy wire and anchor point annotations. Easement exhibit (if prepared) is not reviewed in available documentation.","reasoning":"Down guy anchor easements require 10-foot width and 5-foot extension past anchor entry. Applicability depends on confirming down guys actually exist on poles; current plan documentation is insufficient.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformers (pole-mounted or pad-mounted) are shown on site plan. Proposed electrical design (Sheet 21) shows underground infrastructure with no transformer placement near overhead facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) depicts only underground distribution and pull boxes; no transformers are shown on site.","reasoning":"Transformer clearance from overhead lines applies only when transformers are installed. No transformers are proposed; requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformers or switchgears in niche service configurations are proposed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows only underground service; no niche configurations are depicted.","reasoning":"35-foot niche clearance requirement applies only to niche service configurations. No such installations are proposed.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging areas if shown in project documents"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site logistics plan or construction phasing plan is not included in the available site plan set. Construction staging areas, equipment operation zones, and work platform locations cannot be verified for 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead lines. This requirement will be enforced through construction phase compliance when site logistics plans are submitted.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet index (Sheet 1) lists 39 sheets but no construction phasing, site logistics, or equipment staging plans are included in the reviewed sheet set.","reasoning":"10-foot working clearance from energized overhead lines is an OSHA and construction phase requirement enforced separately from site plan approval. Site plan review cannot verify construction staging clearances without logistics documentation.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction near overhead electric transmission lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 contains 'Electric Transmission Notes' requiring a pre-construction safety meeting with Austin Energy 48 hours before construction, with specific contact information (Andrew Perez, 512-505-7158). OSHA 20-foot working clearance is also documented. Requirement is satisfied for transmission lines. However, if distribution lines (non-transmission) exist on site, separate 48-hour notification to Austin Energy distribution operations may be required; this is not explicitly addressed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 3 found Note #3 in Electric Transmission Notes section stating: '3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7158 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting.'","reasoning":"48-hour notification requirement for transmission lines is satisfied by explicit plan note. UCM § 1.10.2 applies to working clearances near energized overhead lines; transmission line safety meeting meets this intent. If distribution lines exist but voltage is unspecified, distribution line notification requirement is ambiguous.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No service-mast through-roof installations are shown on site plan. Electrical design shows underground service distribution without overhead service drops through building roofs.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) depicts only underground service connections; no roof-penetrating service masts are indicated.","reasoning":"Service-mast roof clearance requirement (3-foot minimum, or 18-inch if within 4 feet of edge) applies only to through-roof installations. No such installations are proposed.","tools_used":["Read"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"1e2ca354-98ec-4708-bfe0-ab48fcb9f00b"}
